TuoVault::withdraw permits zero-output exit swaps for tokens without valuation pools
Description: TuoVaultViews::_exitFloor returns zero when the selected withdrawal token has no valuation
pool.
If the caller also supplies minTokenOut == 0, TuoVault::withdraw executes the exit swap without any
24

minimum output.
This affects configured deposit tokens such as ARB, DAI, and USDC.e, which have no configured valuation pool.
Because supported aggregators encode the recipient in caller-supplied calldata, a malicious frontend can direct
the output elsewhere. The router then measures zero output, but its slippage check passes because the effective
minimum is also zero.
Impact: A malicious frontend can cause a user's entire net withdrawal to be transferred to another recipient
while withdraw returns zero, closes the position, and burns the NFT. The transaction is signed by the user, but it
bypasses the vault-derived floor specifically intended to protect users from unsafe frontend parameters.
