Recommended Mitigation: Apply only the correction named at each cited source location: name the unnamed
mapping value parameter at each row, and at the nested _idle mapping the value parameters of both the inner
and the outer mapping. The pinned compiler accepts a named value parameter on every row, struct-valued and
nested alike, so all of them take the correction directly as written. On the two public rows the chosen name
becomes the output name of the auto-generated getter in the ABI, which is the only externally visible effect of this
change.
