CB-098,FR-231,A large matured position nullifies the bonding period for subsequent deposits,Nethermind__NM0451-1052-FINAL_Vana_Staking.pdf,Nethermind,vana,2026-09-29,yes,yes,2026-09,Medium,"Update from the client 2: Fixed in commit 8b7a3c7.
6.3
[Medium] A large matured position nullifies the bonding period for subsequent
deposits
File(s): /vanaPoolStaking/VanaPoolStakingImplementation.sol
Description: The bonding period is the protocol’s defensive mechanism for discouraging mercenary capital. A staker who exits before it
elapses forfeits their accrued rewards into the entity’s locked pool, which recycles them to the remaining stakers. When capital is added to
an existing position, the contract blends the new bonding requirement with the remaining time on that position, weighted by value.
1
// @audit The full bonding period is divided by the combined value, so a
2
// large existing position shrinks the bond applied to new capital.
3
stakerEntity.rewardEligibilityTimestamp =
4
currentTimestamp + (stakeAmount * bondingPeriod) / newTotalValue;
Because the denominator is the value of the whole combined position, the bonding period applied to the incremental capital is scaled down
by whatever the staker already holds. A staker holding a matured position worth 10000 VANA who then deposits 100 VANA receives a bond
of 25663 seconds, roughly seven hours, instead of the configured 30 days. The larger the existing position, the closer the effective bond is
to zero, and the matured position is unaffected by the operation, so the manoeuvre can be repeated indefinitely. The cost of bootstrapping
the attack is serving the bonding period once.
The redelegate(...) function reproduces the same arithmetic, weighting the incoming amount by its carried remaining bond and the
destination by its own remaining time, and then assigning rather than raising the result.
1
uint256 weightedTime =
2
(existingValue * existingRemaining + movedValue * remainingBond) / newTotalValue;
3
// @audit-issue The blended value is assigned, so an existing bond can be shortened.
4
to.rewardEligibilityTimestamp = currentTimestamp + weightedTime;
Recommendation(s): Consider revisiting the bonding model so that newly added value serves the necessary bonding period on its own
terms. At a minimum, consider ensuring that neither the staking nor the redelegation path can ever move an existing eligibility deadline
earlier than it already was.
Status: Acknowledged
Update from the client:
Acknowledged (WONTFIX): the value-weighted bond blend in stake() / redelegate() intentionally lowers deposit friction for stakers main-
taining large already-bonded capital, weakens only an economic disincentive (no funds at risk, no accounting invariant broken, matured
gains preserved by c583cc7), and the clean per-tranche fix costs storage/complexity or perpetually re-locks honest large stakers — so we
keep it as-is.
