[Medium] Accrued commission can never be withdrawn from the treasury
File(s): /vanaPoolEntity/VanaPoolEntityImplementation.sol, /vanaPoolTreasury/VanaPoolTreasuryImplementation.sol
Description: Each entity may charge a commission, which is an operator cut taken from every reward distribution. The processRewards(...)
function from the VanaPoolEntity contract takes that cut into the accruedCommission field, and the entity owner later withdraws it by calling
the claimCommission(...) function, which instructs the treasury to pay out. All VANA in the system is custodied by the VanaPoolTreasury
contract, and moving funds out of it requires the caller to hold DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE.
1
// @audit-issue The caller of this function is the VanaPoolEntity contract.
2
bool success = vanaPoolStaking.vanaPoolTreasury().transferVana(
3
payable(entity.ownerAddress),
4
amount
5
);
6
if (!success) {
7
revert TransferFailed();
8
}
The treasury grants that role to two addresses when it is initialized, and the updateVanaPool(...) function only rotates it between staking
contracts. The VanaPoolEntity contract is never granted the role.
1
function initialize(address ownerAddress, address vanaPoolAddress) external initializer {
2
// ...
3
_grantRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, ownerAddress);
4
// @audit-issue Only the owner and the staking contract are granted the role.
5
_grantRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, vanaPoolAddress);
6
}
Every reward distribution therefore reduces the delegators’ share by the commission, while every attempt to claim that commission reverts
due to the treasury’s access control check.
Recommendation(s): Consider introducing a dedicated, narrowly scoped spending role on the VanaPoolTreasury contract that gates only
the transfer functionality, and granting it to both the staking and the entity contracts as part of the upgrade procedure. Granting DEFAULT_-
ADMIN_ROLE to the entity contract would also resolve the revert, but it is strongly discouraged, because that role additionally authorizes
upgrades and pausing of the treasury that custodies all staker principal.
Status: Fixed
Update from the client: Fixed (commit 6b7b2d6)
Confirmed real: claimCommission has the entity contract call treasury.transferVana, but transferVana required DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE
and the entity was never granted it, so every claim reverted. (On this branch the same would have broken sweepUnallocatedRewards,
which also pays out through the entity.)
Fix — a narrow SPENDER_ROLE gating only transferVana:
initialize grants SPENDER_ROLE to the staking contract and DEFAULT_ADMIN only to the owner — staking no longer holds admin over
the treasury. updateVanaPool rotates SPENDER_ROLE (not DEFAULT_ADMIN) between staking contracts. New updateVanaPoolEn-
tity(address) (admin-gated) records the entity and grants it SPENDER_ROLE, rotating it off any previous entity — first-class wiring so the
entity’s spend right can’t be silently forgotten. Backed by one appended slot (VanaPoolTreasuryStorageV2).
11

