File(s): ../RewardSplitterImplementation.sol
Description: The RewardSplitterImplementation contract includes a buy-and-burn mechanism that sets aside a portion of the distributed
tokens to be burned later. The executeBuyAndBurn() function is responsible for executing this burn by transferring the accrued native
tokens. However, the function sends these funds to a configurable sink address rather than address(0).
The protocol’s burn mechanism is intended to reduce the totalSupply of tokens in order to increase the price per token. Because the
current logic transfers the tokens to a ""sink"" address instead of the zero address, the tokens are never actually destroyed. Consequently,
the totalSupply does not change, meaning the feature is broken and will not achieve its desired economic goal.
1
