6.14
[Low] The maximum unstake view simulates only the APY reward model
File(s): contracts/vanaStaking/vanaPoolStaking/VanaPoolStakingImplementation.sol
Description: The getMaxUnstakeAmount(...) function from the VanaPoolStaking contract tells an integrator how much a staker can
withdraw right now. Its documentation states that it simulates reward settlement in order to quote accurate share prices, and front ends
are expected to size withdrawals from the values it returns.
The simulation reproduces only one of the two reward models, and omits the operator commission entirely.
1
// @audit-issue The APY formula is applied unconditionally, with no check of the
2
// @audit-issue entity's reward model and no deduction for commission.
3
