Update from the client:
Update from Nethermind: fixed at commit.
Update from Nethermind#2: the minStakeAmount is not enforced on the unstake && redelegate paths. A user can unstake or redelegate
such that they will end up with a position that’s below minStakeAmount.
Update from the client: Fixed (7752e34). minStakeAmount is now enforced on exit paths as well: a partial unstake/unstakeVana must
leave nothing or a position worth at least the minimum, and redelegate must move at least the minimum and leave nothing or at least the
minimum in the source. Full exits remain unrestricted. Registration floors exceed the minimum on both chains, so registrants are never
trapped between the two rules. Tests in MinStakeResidual.t.sol.
Update from Nethermind#3 (Telegram): Now in legacy pools, if someone have a position which is worth less than minShareAmount,
they won’t be able to delegate their position and will need to unstake in order to stake in different pool. It can be intended design choice
though.
Update from the client: Agreed and refined (7171d8b). A whole-position redelegation is now always allowed, so a legacy position below
the minimum can still migrate (relocating it creates no dust); only splitting a position must respect minStakeAmount on both the moved
and the residual side. Full exits remain unrestricted. Test test_fullRedelegateOfASubMinimumLegacyPositionIsAllowed.
