NM-1048 — INFRARED ROUTER — SECURITY REVIEW
6.5
[Info] Multiswap events sum input amounts across tokens with different deci-
mals
File(s): src/Router.sol
Description: The swapMulti(...) function accepts several input tokens and several output tokens in one transaction, and emits one Swap
event per output. The event carries a single input token and a single input amount, and its documentation states that the ten fields are
sufficient to reconstruct full fee attribution off chain.
The values placed in those two fields are produced by accumulating across every input:
1
uint256 n = params.inputTokens.length;
2
// @audit-issue One arbitrary token is chosen to label the aggregate.
3
effectiveInputToken = params.inputTokens[0];
4
address exec = executor;
5
for (uint256 i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
6
address token = params.inputTokens[i];
7
// @audit-issue Amounts of different tokens are summed into one scalar.
8
inputAmountSum += params.inputAmounts[i];
9
// ...
10
if (token == NATIVE_ETH_SENTINEL) {
11
nativeForwardAmount = forward;
12
effectiveInputToken = NATIVE_ETH_SENTINEL;
13
}
14
}
Adding an amount denominated in a six decimal token to one denominated in an eighteen decimal token produces a wrong number and
labelling it with whichever token occupies the first slot makes it misleading. For inputs of 10_000e6 USDC and 1e18 WETH the emitted
amount is 1000000010000000000 tagged as USDC, and WETH is absent from every event the swap produces.
This means the documented reconstruction does not hold for multi input swap.
The failure is silent because the ratio between the
aggregated fee and the aggregated amount still approximates the configured basis points, so a check on the implied rate passes while
every consumer that reads the amounts as values is wrong by the decimal difference between the tokens. Any off chain process that relies
on these numbers will be wrong.
Recommendation(s): Consider emitting a dedicated multi swap event that carries the input token and amount arrays and compute the
amounts accordingly.
Status: Fixed at commit 54435a9
Update from the client: Fixed in commit 54435a9. Multi-swaps now emit a single MultiSwap event carrying parallel per-token arrays (input
tokens and amounts, per-input protocol and partner fees, output tokens, gross and net outputs, per-output partner fees and captured
slippage). Nothing is summed or split across tokens, and Swap is emitted only by the single-swap entry points. The pro-rata splitting
helpers were removed. Covered by a mixed-decimals test (10_000e6 + 1e18 inputs with fees and captured slippage) that checks every
emitted value against on-chain balances.
11

