}
The swap is an exact input trade for amountIn, Uniswap V4 opens a debt for the specified amountIn. The SETTLE_ALL action reads that
debt, confirms it does not exceed the supplied maximum, and settles it by having Permit2 pull funds from the helper. There are two places
where this can revert, depending on whether the helper happens to hold enough token balance:
−The helper holds only what arrived. The Permit2 pull asks the token to move amountIn out of a contract holding amountIn minus
the transfer fee, so the token’s own transferFrom fails. The transaction reverts inside the Permit2 transfer;
−The helper holds enough to cover the shortfall. The pull succeeds, but the transfer into the pool manager will withold another fee.
Uniswap V4 credits only what arrived and the _settle(...) function computes paid as the difference between its synced reserves
and its balance afterwards. The amount transferred is not enough to cover the debt and Uniswap reverts with CurrencyNotSettled;
Recommendation(s): The protocol would have to precompute all the fees offchain and build the weiroll command in a way that accounts
for all the transfers and their fees in ordered for the swap to succeed.
Status: Acknowledged
Update from the client: Won’t fix. Fee-on-transfer tokens are unsupported by decision. Natspec that implied support (Router _pullInput
/ _pullInputViaPermit2, FR-15) was corrected and the same statement added to UniswapV4SwapHelpers in commit d9b6dbb. No logic
changes.
13

