with the exact Universal Router the deploy script pins and run a real USDC -> USDT swap; all three pass against the pinned 2.1.1 routers.
./deploy.sh deploy|dry-run now runs the target chain’s layout test as a gate and refuses to proceed if it fails or cannot run. The guard
uses an ERC20/ERC20 pool deliberately: with the legacy 5-field router, native ETH pools succeed by accident (the misread hookData
offset lands on currency0 == address(0)), while USDC -> USDT reverts, which we verified against the legacy mainnet router. Adding a
chain now requires a matching layout test.
