existing tests assert the certificate comes back to the customer, so returning it is deliberate and this is
a product decision, not just a code change.
Option B, mark it spent (recommended). Add a Redeemed state and park the certificate there instead of
returning it to the depositable state. Deposits then reject it automatically. Add a certifier only function
that moves it back to usable, but only when a new one time custody proof is supplied, the same
standard as a first deposit. The customer keeps the certificate as a document travelling with their bar, it
just cannot create money until someone confirms the bar is back.
Either way, add a test asserting a returned certificate cannot mint TROY again, and expose a way to
check on chain whether a certificate has been redeemed.
