- address admin = ADMIN; address upgrader = ADMIN; address operator = ADMIN;
- address certifier = ADMIN; address custodian = ADMIN;
+ address admin     = vm.envAddress(""VAULT_ADMIN"");
+ address upgrader  = vm.envAddress(""VAULT_UPGRADER"");
+ address operator  = vm.envAddress(""VAULT_OPERATOR"");
+ address certifier = vm.envAddress(""VAULT_CERTIFIER"");
+ address custodian = vm.envAddress(""VAULT_CUSTODIAN"");
+ _requireDistinct([admin, upgrader, operator, certifier, custodian]);
+ require(currentVault.totalBackedOzMicro() == 0 && currentVault.pendingRequests() == 0
+     && currentVault.totalLockedTroy() == 0, ""outgoing vault not drained"");
  vm.startBroadcast();
- currentVault.pause();
+ // deploy and verify the replacement first, then pause
Add the drained vault precondition, and see Finding 2, because that check alone can leave you with a
vault that can never be replaced.
Reorder so the replacement is deployed and verified before the live system is paused. Even though the
current failure mode is harmless, ""pause production first, build the replacement second"" is the wrong
order and will eventually bite.
Finally, either give this script the same explicit ""not for deployment"" header its sibling carries, or make it
actually work. Right now it advertises itself as a live migration path and is not one.
Status
Acknowledged
Team’s Comment
DeployAndWireVaultSingleAdmin.s.sol is a test script and will not be used for the main
deployment. Its header already describes a test migration.
