Impact
The creator captures accrued LP fees at up to the pre-ratchet share 70% instead of 60%, 50%, or
40% on the whole uncollected backlog. This is a permanent misallocation of protocol revenue
against the schedule the ratchet exists to enforce, recurring at each of the three thresholds on
every launch. No user principal is at risk and no user is denied an action, which is what keeps this
below High.
Likelihood
High. Both legs are permissionless, neither requires capital or a privileged role, the ordering is
trivially automatable, and the profitable ordering is the one the creator wants.
Recommendation
Have LPLocker.collect() call LPFeeRatchet.poke(launchToken) before harvesting. Both functions
are already permissionless, so this adds no trust assumption and no new authority, and it closes
the ordering race completely:
Alternatively, accrue LP fees against the tier in effect at accrual time rather than at collection
time.
