CrackerSwap Team’s Comment
We believe the recommended fix is unsafe and have not implemented it. eth_estimateGas binary-
searches for the cheapest gas that succeeds; if a close that skipped settlement succeeded,
every wallet would converge on that path and settlement would never fire in production, reopening
the window between curve close and pool open that atomic settlement exists to eliminate. This is
invariant I16, asserted in fork/LifecycleFailures.fork.ts by sending the closing buy at the wallet's
own gas estimate against live Uniswap V4. A closer rebate from the graduation fee was also
rejected: it would place an ETH transfer to an arbitrary address inside _settle, letting a closer with
a reverting receive() force a deferral, so any future version must be pull-payment. The issue is
instead answered operationally: a Graduate button on any CLOSED curve gated on the module's
migrationReady() view, the creator as the natural closer since LP fees do not accrue until the pool
