11. Quote views return live-looking numbers after graduation
Resolved
Path
contracts/BondingCurve.sol
Function Name
reserves(), quoteBuy(), quoteSell(), tokensSold()
_settle() zeroes the curve's real quote reserve (BondingCurve.sol:419) but does not reset
tokensSold. The views reserves(), quoteBuy(), quoteSell() and tokensSold() are not phase-gated
(:210-252), so after graduation they compute against a retained tokensSold and a zeroed reserve.
reserves(), for instance, returns the virtual quote and a token reserve that still looks live for a
curve that can no longer trade.
Impact
Off-chain integrators reading the views without checking phase() will display incorrect post-
graduation pricing, which presents as an apparent price spike. We confirmed there is no on-chain
consumer of these views anywhere outside BondingCurve itself, so no funds are affected; every
value-moving entry point is phase-gated.
Likelihood
Medium for naive integrators; zero on-chain impact.
Recommendation
Document that the views are meaningful only during TRADING, or have them return zeroed values
once the curve has graduated.
