14. Curve initialisation has no caller restriction 
CrackerSwap Team’s Comment
The recommended guard reads the p.factory parameter rather than storage, so it provides no
protection: an attacker front-running a future two-step factory would simply pass their own
address as p.factory and the guard would pass. A real guard requires the factory to be fixed at
clone time, as an immutable on the implementation, which is a design change for a currently
unreachable issue. The protection remains architectural: createLaunch clones and initialises the
curve in a single transaction.
