16. seededAt is write-only state with no internal
consumer
Acknowledged
Path
contracts/hooks/AntiSnipeHook.sol
Function Name
_beforeAddLiquidity(), poolOf()
seededAt is declared (AntiSnipeHook.sol:42) and written once (:145) but is never read by any logic.
It is observable only through the poolOf getter, and occupies space in the packed pool-state slot.
Impact
None functionally; minor gas and storage cost, plus the documentation implication that something
consumes it.
Likelihood
Not applicable; the field is unused on every launch.
Recommendation
Remove the field, which repacks the slot, or consume it, for example by exposing the seeding time
in an event.
CrackerSwap Team’s Comment
seededAt is part of the backend data surface. It was introduced in commit 9882486 (""record the
backend's data surface on-chain"") together with lockedAt, registeredAt, graduatedAt and
recoveryOpenedAt, to hold data the indexer would otherwise reconstruct from log history. It has an
external consumer by design, and it rides in bytes already paid for, so it costs a shift and an OR
rather than an SSTORE.
