CrackerSwap Audit Report
Functional Tests
Functional Tests
Functional Tests
A launch can be created, seeded by the creator, traded, and graduated end to end, with the V4 pool
opening at exactly the price the curve closed at.
The closing buy settles atomically: fee deposit, proportional burn, pool initialisation, full-range mint,
and NFT handoff all occur in one transaction or none do.
seedBuy is rejected from any caller other than the factory, and from any curve where tokensSold != 0.
initialize is one-shot; every non-UNINITIALIZED phase rejects re-initialisation, and invalid parameter
domains are rejected before a launch becomes live.
Buy and sell quotes round against the trader in both directions; the constant product k is non-
decreasing across every buy, sell, and round trip.
A crossing buy is capped at exactly graduationTarget, with the excess refunded to msg.sender and the
tokens delivered to beneficiary.
realQuote tracks the curve's native balance exactly across arbitrary trade sequences; the curve has
no receive/fallback, so force-fed ETH cannot enter pricing.
A settlement failure with non-empty revert data emits GraduationDeferred and leaves the curve
CLOSED and retryable; graduate() then succeeds permissionlessly.
enterRecovery() reverts before the full 7-day delay without touching any state, and after it burns
exactly lpSupply + (curveSupply − tokensSold).
RECOVERY redemption is pro-rata and cannot overdraw the opening reserve across any partition of
sellers.
The anti-snipe fee decays linearly from startFee to floorFee across the window, and an unarmed pool
fails open to the floor fee.
Pool initialisation for a launch's key is rejected from any sender other than the migration module.
www.quillaudits.com
57

CrackerSwap Audit Report
Functional Tests
The locker accepts a position only from the migration module, in a pool carrying this locker's hook,
dynamic fee, and the configured tick spacing; a re-lock of an already-held position is rejected.
collect() never removes liquidity — the encoded DECREASE_LIQUIDITY amount is asserted zero — and a
locked position never leaves the locker.
Splitter claims are pull-based and consume only the caller's own entry; a deposit for one launch
cannot credit another launch's creator.
ratchetDown accepts only the immutable ratchet address and only a strict decrease to a named tier.
The ratchet's window matures on observed (swap-advanced) time rather than wall-clock time; a short or
unchanged hook clock reverts atomically and preserves the original anchor.
Fork tests pin the settlement gas cost (650,781) against the 800,000 MIN_SETTLE_GAS floor and assert
that an under-gassed closing buy reverts rather than quietly skipping settlement.
BondingCurve.sol
balance never falls below realQuote across buys, sells, refunds, force-feed, donations (fuzzed)
[...excerpt ends]"
