Description
Staking rewards governance participation with a temporary APY boost. The owner calls
submitGovernanceEligible with a list of backend userId s, and for each one governanceBonusUntil
is set to the current time plus 90 days. During that window every position of the userId should earn
the tier's base APY plus GOV_BONUS_BPS , which is 1%. Outside the window it should earn the base APY
only. The contract stores just the end timestamp. It does not record when the grant started.
Rewards are not streamed. They are settled lazily when _accrueStakeFor runs for a position, which
happens through unstake , unstakeEarly , partialUnstake , withdraw , accelerateCooldown and
claimMonthlyRewards . At settlement, _computeRewardForUserId charges simple interest on principal
for the whole interval since lastAccrualTimestamp . It gets the rate from _effectiveAPYBpsForUserId ,
which calls StakingLibrary.effectiveAPY . That function only checks whether the current block.
timestamp is earlier than governanceBonusUntil and, if so, adds the 1% bonus. It never compares the
bonus window with the interval being settled. So whether the bonus applies is decided once, at the
moment of settlement, and then used for the entire elapsed interval. That interval can go back months
before the grant. The monthly steps inside the auto-compound loop of _accrueStakeFor have the same
