www.quillaudits.com

Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
M-01
Governance-eligible stakers earn the bonus APY on time before it
was granted via settlement-time APY lookup in
_effectiveAPYBpsForUserId 
Assume a total supply of 1,000,000,000 LRY and a user with one 10,000,000 LRY Premium position (1%
of supply, so the whale multiplier is 1.0x) earning the 12% base APY. The position was last accrued 300
days ago. The owner then grants the user governance eligibility. Within the next 90 days, the user calls
any function that accrues the position, for example claimMonthlyRewards . The full 300 days are priced
at 13% instead of 12%, which credits 82,191 LRY of bonus for time before the grant existed. The real 90
day bonus on this position is worth only 24,657 LRY, so the user receives more than three times the
intended amount. The longer a position goes without accruing before a grant, the larger the windfall. A
staker who expects to be granted eligibility can deliberately avoid touching their positions to maximise
it.
The reverse also happens. If a granted user does not accrue the position before governanceBonusUntil
passes, the next settlement prices the whole interval at the base APY. The bonus they earned during the
90 day window disappears completely. The same position above would lose the full 24,657 LRY.
As a result, the bonus a staker receives depends on when they happen to settle, not on whether they
were eligible during the time being paid for. Early settlers are overpaid from the shared reward pool and
late settlers are underpaid.
Impact
Medium
A granted staker who settles inside the bonus window collects the 1% bonus over their entire unsettled
history. In the example above that is 82,191 LRY instead of the intended 24,657 LRY, an overpayment of
57,534 LRY taken from the reward pool funded through depositRewards . A granted staker who settles
only after the window ends loses the whole bonus they earned. Principal is not affected. The loss or
windfall is limited to yield and scales with position size and the length of the unsettled interval.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Apply the governance bonus only to the part of each accrual interval that overlaps the bonus window,
for example by tracking the grant start time or by settling all of the user's positions when a grant is
made or ends.
(continued)
