Medium Severity Issues
M-02
Premium stakers halve the early-exit penalty via near-
total withdrawal in partialUnstake
Resolved
Path
contracts/Staking.sol, contracts/libraries/StakingLibrary.sol
Function Name
partialUnstake(), unstakeEarly()
Description
Staking offers Premium stakers two ways out before the lock-up ends. unstakeEarly closes the whole
position. It charges the tier's earlyExitPenalty , which initialize sets to 5% for Premium, forfeits
every accrued reward, marks the position earlyExited , and moves the remaining 95% into cooldown.
partialUnstake is meant as a lighter option for trimming a position while keeping the rest locked, and
it becomes available 90 days after startTime ( PARTIAL_UNSTAKE_EARLIEST ). It charges PARTIAL_
UNSTAKE_PENALTY_BPS , which is 2.5%, on the slice being withdrawn. It forfeits only that slice's
proportional share of rewardAccrued , sends the forfeited reward to insuranceReserve , and moves the
rest of the slice into cooldown. The remaining principal stays staked and can be unstaked normally once
the lock ends.
The only limit partialUnstake puts on the slice size is that amount must be greater than zero and
strictly less than pos.principal . Nothing sets a maximum fraction, and nothing requires the remainder
to stay at or above minStake or any other meaningful size. A Premium staker can therefore pass an
amount equal to the full principal minus one wei. The contract treats that as a partial exit, charges 2.5%
instead of 5%, and leaves a one-wei position behind. In economic terms that is a full early exit.
withdraw then pays out the cooldown slice, and the one-wei remainder either sits there or is unstaked
for free once the lock ends.
Take a Premium staker with 1,000,000 LRY who wants out 100 days into a 12 month lock. Through
unstakeEarly they pay a 50,000 LRY penalty to penaltyReceiver and get 950,000 LRY back after
the cooldown. If they instead call partialUnstake for 1,000,000 LRY minus one wei, the penalty is
about 25,000 LRY and about 975,000 LRY enters cooldown. Almost all of the accrued reward is forfeited
either way, because the forfeited share is proportional and the slice is nearly 100% of principal. The
cooldown length is also the same, since both paths use the tier cooldown and neither qualifies for
acceleration. The only real difference is that the staker keeps 25,000 LRY of penalty that the protocol
should have collected. Any Premium staker past day 90 can do this with no special setup.
