Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
M-02
Premium stakers halve the early-exit penalty via near-total
withdrawal in partialUnstake 
So the 5% Premium early-exit penalty becomes a 2.5% penalty for every exit after day 90. That
undercuts the lock-up commitment Premium's higher APY is meant to pay for, and diverts half of the
expected penalty revenue away from penaltyReceiver .
Impact
Medium
Every Premium staker who exits early after day 90 can avoid half the intended early-exit penalty, which
is 2.5% of their principal (25,000 LRY on a 1,000,000 LRY position). The staker keeps that amount and
the protocol's penaltyReceiver loses it. User principal is never at risk. The loss is penalty revenue only,
and it repeats for every Premium early exit.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Require the remainder after partialUnstake to stay above a meaningful minimum, such as minStake ,
or cap the share of principal a single partial unstake can remove, so that a near-total exit has to go
through unstakeEarly .
