Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
M-03
Deployer can permanently lock ICO and Vesting admin
functions via missing zero-address check on _owner in
initialize
Resolved
Path
contracts/ICO.sol, contracts/Vesting.sol
Function Name
initialize()
Description
LendaryICO and LendaryVesting are deployed behind proxies, so their real setup happens in
initialize rather than in the constructor. Each constructor runs Ownable(_msgSender()) and
_disableInitializers() , but that only affects the implementation contract's own storage. The proxy
starts with no owner. It gets its owner only when initialize ends by calling _transferOwnership(
_owner) . Every privileged action in both contracts uses the onlyOwner modifier. In LendaryICO these
are sendLeftoverTokens , updateReceiverAddress , setKycSigner and setUserPrice . In
LendaryVesting they are registerPrivateSaleUser , sendLeftoverTokens , updateReceiverAddress
and setKycSigner .
Neither initialize checks that _owner is a non-zero address. The OpenZeppelin Ownable used here
only rejects the zero address in its constructor and in the public transferOwnership . The internal
_transferOwnership that initialize calls accepts address zero without complaint. So if the
deployment script passes a zero _owner , through an unset environment variable or a wrong argument
order, initialization succeeds and the proxy ends up with owner() equal to address zero. The
initializer modifier blocks a second call to initialize , and nobody can call transferOwnership
because no one is the owner. The Staking contract shows the intended pattern: its initialize rejects
a zero _admin with ZeroAdmin . The other two contracts do not.
After a bad initialization, every owner function in both contracts is unreachable. In LendaryICO , unsold
LRY from the 50,000,000 LRY sale allocation cannot be recovered with sendLeftoverTokens . The
hardcoded receiverAddress can never be changed. Per-user prices cannot be set. A compromised KYC
signer cannot be rotated, so whoever holds that key could keep approving purchases indefinitely. In
LendaryVesting , registerPrivateSaleUser can never run, so the private sale cannot onboard anyone.
Unallocated private-sale LRY is stuck, and the treasury address and KYC signer are frozen as well.
23
www.quillaudits.com

Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
M-03
Deployer can permanently lock ICO and Vesting admin functions
via missing zero-address check on _owner in initialize 
So a single bad constructor argument leaves both contracts without an admin. The only way to recover
is a proxy upgrade that adds a new initializer, and that is possible only if the proxy admin was set up
correctly and separately.
Impact
Medium
If _owner is set to zero, all admin functionality in LendaryICO and LendaryVesting is lost. Unsold ICO
tokens (up to the full 50,000,000 LRY allocation) and unallocated private-sale tokens stay locked in the
contracts. The private sale cannot run, and the KYC signer and treasury address cannot be changed. The
situation can only be fixed through a proxy upgrade by the proxy admin.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Reject a zero _owner in initialize for both LendaryICO and LendaryVesting , the same way
Staking validates its admin.
(continued)
