_accrueStakeFor, _adjustObligated, rescueERC20
Description
Staking holds two kinds of LRY in one balance: what it owes stakers (active principal, cooldown
principal and accrued rewards) and spare reward funding the owner adds through depositRewards . The
private counter _totalObligated tracks the first kind. _openStakePosition adds the staked amount,
accruing rewards adds the reward, and payouts, penalties and fees subtract what leaves the contract,
all through _adjustObligated . rescueERC20 relies on this counter. When the owner tries to pull LRY
out, it reverts with WouldUnderfund unless the contract's LRY balance stays at or above
_totalObligated plus the amount being rescued. The design rule is that _totalObligated always
equals what stakers are actually owed.
When monthly auto-compound is on for a position, _accrueStakeFor handles each monthly step in two
stages. First it computes stepReward for the interval up to the month boundary, adds it to pos.
rewardAccrued , and calls _adjustObligated with plus stepReward . That correctly records the new
liability. Then it takes the whole of pos.rewardAccrued as r , which includes the stepReward just
recorded and any earlier accrued reward that was also recorded when it accrued. It moves r into pos.
principal and resets rewardAccrued to zero. But it also calls _adjustObligated again with plus r .
Moving value from rewardAccrued into principal does not change how much the contract owes; it only
reclassifies a liability that is already counted. Adding r a second time means every compounded token
is counted twice. Exits only subtract what is actually paid: _settleCooldownExit subtracts
netPrincipal + reward , and penalties and forfeits are subtracted when they are sent out. So the extra
copy of each compounded reward is never removed and builds up permanently in _totalObligated .
