Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
M-05
Owner cannot rescue surplus LRY because _accrueStakeFor counts
each compounded reward twice in _totalObligated 
For example, a single Premium position of 10,000,000 LRY at 12% APY with auto-compound on
compounds 11 times over a 12 month lock and folds in about 1,156,000 LRY of rewards. _totalObligated
is overstated by that same 1,156,000 LRY. Even after the staker unstakes and withdraws everything, the
counter still reports 1,156,000 LRY owed to no one. Across all auto-compounding positions, the
overstatement grows with every monthly step. Any spare reward funding up to that amount is then
blocked by rescueERC20 . Once the overstatement exceeds the spare balance, the owner cannot rescue
any LRY at all, even when nothing is owed to stakers.
So the contract's own record of what it owes no longer matches reality. The safety check meant to
protect staker funds instead traps the protocol's surplus LRY with no way to correct the counter.
Impact
Medium
Protocol-owned LRY equal to the total of all compounded rewards becomes impossible to recover
through rescueERC20 , for example about 1,156,000 LRY for a single 10,000,000 LRY Premium position
compounding over one year. The lockup is permanent because _totalObligated can only be changed
by real flows and has no admin correction. Staker funds are not at risk, because subtractions never
exceed real liabilities, so user payouts never underflow.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Do not adjust _totalObligated when moving accrued rewards into principal during auto-compound,
since the liability was already recorded when the reward accrued.
(continued)
