Lendary - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
M-06
Stakers lose or gain rewards they already earned because
_refreshMultipliersOfUserId changes the whale multiplier before accruing
them 
Here is how an ordinary staker loses out. Assume a total supply of 1,000,000,000 LRY and two Premium
positions for one userId totalling 10,000,000 LRY, or 1% of supply, so both run at 1.0x. The user leaves
them alone for 180 days. At the 12% Premium APY they have earned 591,780 LRY, but none of it is
checkpointed. The user then opens a third position of 5,000,000 LRY, which passes both the velocity
cap and the 2% position cap. The aggregate rises to 15,000,000 LRY and
_refreshMultipliersOfUserId sets both older positions to 0.85x. When they next accrue, the 180 days
already earned are paid at 0.85x, which is 503,013 LRY. The user silently loses 88,767 LRY that they
earned before the new stake existed.
A staker can also use this on purpose to gain. Take a user whose aggregate is 15,000,000 LRY (0.85x),
made up of 10,000,000 LRY in long-lock Premium positions and a 5,000,000 LRY Base position with a
shorter lock. The user never touches the Premium positions. Once the Base lock ends, the user calls
unstake on it and then withdraw . _settleCooldownExit lowers the aggregate to 10,000,000 LRY, and
_refreshMultipliersOfUserId sets the untouched Premium positions back to 1.0x. If they went 180
days without accruing, every one of those days is now paid at 1.0x instead of the 0.85x that applied. The
user takes 88,767 LRY more than the protocol's rules allow, out of the reward pool shared with other
stakers. A smaller version of this happens whenever a partialUnstake or unstakeEarly penalty lowers
the aggregate.
In short, rewards depend on the order and timing of a user's actions rather than on how much they
actually staked over time. Honest multi-position stakers lose yield they already earned, and anyone who
plans their exits can push the anti-whale discount off their past yield.
Impact
Medium
Stakers with several positions whose aggregate sits between 1% and 2% of supply lose earned rewards
when they add stake. In the example above that is 88,767 LRY, or 15% of 180 days of yield on 10,000,000
LRY. A user who sequences exits deliberately can claim the same amount in excess rewards from the
shared reward pool. Principal is never at risk. The damage is limited to mispriced yield and scales with
position size, time left unaccrued, and the size of the multiplier change, up to the full 30% band.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Accrue all active positions of a userId at their current multiplier before _refreshMultipliersOfUserId
changes it, so that each new multiplier only applies to rewards earned from that point on.
(continued)
30
