Lendary - Audit Report
Low Severity Issues
Low Severity Issues
L-02
KYC signatures have no expiration and no amount in
_verifyAndConsumeKycSignature
Acknowledged
Path
contracts/KycSignatureGate.sol
Function Name
_verifyAndConsumeKycSignature()
Description
stake in Staking and buyTokens in ICO both require a backend KYC signature, which
_verifyAndConsumeKycSignature checks. The signed message covers only the userId , the wallet, the
wallet's current entry in kycNonces , the chain id and the contract address. It has no expiration
timestamp and no amount.
Because there is no expiration, a signature stays valid until it is used, no matter how much time has
passed. A user can get a signature, hold it, and use it weeks or months later, even after the backend
would no longer approve them. Because there is no amount, the same signature works for a stake or
purchase of any size, so the backend cannot limit what it approves.
Impact
Low
An old or no longer intended signature can still be used to stake or buy any amount within the on-chain
limits. No funds are lost directly. The backend's only way to cancel an unused signature is to rotate
kycSigner , which cancels every user's outstanding signatures at once.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Add an expiration timestamp and the approved amount to the signed message, and check both on-chain.
33
www.quillaudits.com

Lendary - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-01
Owner can lose admin control permanently through
single-step transferOwnership and renounceOwnership
Resolved
Path
contracts/Staking.sol, contracts/Vesting.sol, contracts/ICO.sol, 
contracts/LRYToken.sol, contracts/stLRY.sol
Function Name
transferOwnership(), renounceOwnership()
Description
Staking , Vesting , ICO and LRYToken inherit OpenZeppelin Ownable . There, transferOwnership
moves ownership to the new address immediately, without the new owner having to accept it. If the
owner types a wrong or unreachable address, ownership is lost for good. None of the five contracts
overrides renounceOwnership , so one accidental call sets the owner to the zero address. That includes
stLRY , which already uses the two-step Ownable2Step .
Losing ownership permanently disables every onlyOwner function: pausing, rotating the KYC signer,
depositing staking rewards, toggling auto-compound, updating receivers and rescuing tokens.
Impact
Low
An owner mistake would permanently remove admin control over the protocol, including emergency
pause. No user can exploit this.
Likelihood
Low
Recommendation
Use Ownable2Step in all contracts and override renounceOwnership to revert.
34
www.quillaudits.com

