CB-166,,I-01 Owner can lose admin control permanently through single-step transferOwnership and renounceOwnership,QuillAudits__Lendary_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,lendary,2026-09-23,no,no,2026-10,Informational,"Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-01
Owner can lose admin control permanently through
single-step transferOwnership and renounceOwnership
Resolved
Path
contracts/Staking.sol, contracts/Vesting.sol, contracts/ICO.sol, 
contracts/LRYToken.sol, contracts/stLRY.sol
Function Name
transferOwnership(), renounceOwnership()
Description
Staking , Vesting , ICO and LRYToken inherit OpenZeppelin Ownable . There, transferOwnership
moves ownership to the new address immediately, without the new owner having to accept it. If the
owner types a wrong or unreachable address, ownership is lost for good. None of the five contracts
overrides renounceOwnership , so one accidental call sets the owner to the zero address. That includes
stLRY , which already uses the two-step Ownable2Step .
Losing ownership permanently disables every onlyOwner function: pausing, rotating the KYC signer,
depositing staking rewards, toggling auto-compound, updating receivers and rescuing tokens.
Impact
Low
An owner mistake would permanently remove admin control over the protocol, including emergency
pause. No user can exploit this.
Likelihood
Low
Recommendation
Use Ownable2Step in all contracts and override renounceOwnership to revert.
34
www.quillaudits.com

Lendary - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-02
Enhanced stakers with the governance bonus earn
above the tier maxAPY cap because effectiveAPY ignores it
Resolved
Path
contracts/libraries/StakingLibrary.sol, contracts/Staking.sol
Function Name
effectiveAPY(), _effectiveAPYBpsForUserId()
Description
Each tier in tierConfig stores a baseAPY and a maxAPY , and maxAPY is documented as the maximum,
governance-boosted APY for that tier. _effectiveAPYBpsForUserId passes only baseAPY to
effectiveAPY . That function adds the 1% GOV_BONUS_BPS when the user's governance bonus is active
and returns the sum without comparing it with maxAPY . maxAPY is never read anywhere in the
contracts.
With the configured values, Base reaches 8% + 1% = 9%, exactly its cap. Premium reaches 12% + 1% =
13%, below its 13.6% cap. Enhanced reaches 9.6% + 1% = 10.6%, which is above its 10.4% cap. Every
Enhanced position whose userId has the governance bonus therefore earns more than the tier's
intended maximum.
Impact
Low
Enhanced stakers with an active governance bonus earn 0.2% APY more than the documented cap, paid
from the protocol's reward funds. The overpayment is small and stops when the 90 day bonus expires.
Likelihood
Low
Recommendation
Cap the effective APY at the tier's maxAPY in effectiveAPY .
35
