CB-169,,Blacklist controls can permanently freeze pool-held tMUSD,QuillAudits__RapidDex_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,rapiddex,2026-08-25,no,no,2026-11,Medium,"Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
Blacklist controls can permanently freeze pool-held
tMUSD
Acknowledged
Path
TestToken.sol
Function Name
blacklist(), _update()
Description
blacklist() can target any non-zero address, including V3 pools. Once a pool is blacklisted, _update()
rejects outbound tMUSD transfers from that pool.
Impact
Swaps, burns, fee collection, and LP exits that need the pool to send tMUSD can stop working, stranding
pooled user capital.
Recommendation
Protect protocol-critical addresses from blacklist actions or require delayed governance approval with a
documented recovery path.
14
www.quillaudits.com

RapidDex - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
Blacklisted infinite spenders can continue using existing
allowances
Resolved
Path
TestToken.sol
Function Name
transferFrom(), _spendAllowance(), _approve()
Description
The blacklist checks from, to, and allowance writes, but not the spender in transferFrom(). OpenZeppelin
skips _approve() when allowance is type(uint256).max.
Impact
A blacklisted spender with pre-existing infinite approval can keep pulling tokens from non-blacklisted
users and cannot be revoked with approve(spender, 0).
Recommendation
Check notBlacklisted(msg.sender) in transferFrom() or _spendAllowance(), including the infinite-
allowance branch.
15
www.quillaudits.com

RapidDex - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
Paused tMUSD can be made permanently unresumable
through ownership renunciation
Resolved
Path
TestToken.sol, Ownable.sol
Function Name
pause(), unpause(), renounceOwnership()
Description
pause() and unpause() are owner-only, but inherited renounceOwnership() can remove the owner forever.
Impact
If tMUSD is paused before ownership is renounced or the owner key is lost, transfers, mints, burns,
swaps, and LP exits can remain frozen permanently.
Recommendation
Disable renounceOwnership() or replace the single owner with recoverable multisig or governance-
controlled roles.
16
www.quillaudits.com

RapidDex - Audit Report
Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
Non-zero allowance resets expose users to old-plus-new
allowance spending
Resolved
Path
WMST.sol, TestToken.sol
Function Name
approve(), transferFrom()
Description
Both tokens allow a non-zero allowance to be overwritten with another non-zero allowance.
Impact
With a sandwich operation, an approved spender can spend the old allowance before the reset lands,
then spend the new allowance after it lands.
Recommendation
Require non-zero allowance changes to pass through zero, or expose safer increase and decrease
allowance flows with SafeERC20.
17
