CB-170,,Blacklisted infinite spenders can continue using existing allowances,QuillAudits__RapidDex_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,rapiddex,2026-08-25,no,no,2026-11,Medium,"Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
Blacklisted infinite spenders can continue using existing
allowances
Resolved
Path
TestToken.sol
Function Name
transferFrom(), _spendAllowance(), _approve()
Description
The blacklist checks from, to, and allowance writes, but not the spender in transferFrom(). OpenZeppelin
skips _approve() when allowance is type(uint256).max.
Impact
A blacklisted spender with pre-existing infinite approval can keep pulling tokens from non-blacklisted
users and cannot be revoked with approve(spender, 0).
Recommendation
Check notBlacklisted(msg.sender) in transferFrom() or _spendAllowance(), including the infinite-
allowance branch.
