TBC Token - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Tokens sent to the token contract's own address are locked forever
Recommendation
Reject transfers to the token's own address. In OpenZeppelin v5 this takes one override of the _update
hook that every transfer passes through:
function _update(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal override 
{
    require(to != address(this), ""cannot send to token contract"");
    super._update(from, to, value);
}
This is a fixed rule that nobody can change after deployment. It is not a blacklist and gives no address
any special power. If the team prefers to keep the contract exactly as it is, the contract address should
be published with a clear note that it is not a deposit address.
(continued)
