TBC Token - Audit Report
Threat Model
Threat Model
1. External Dependencies & Trust Boundaries
This section enumerates everything the protocol does not fully control.
TBCToken is a standalone token. It does not call any external contract, holds no other project's tokens,
and reads no oracle or price feed. Everything it depends on is either an OpenZeppelin base contract
compiled into it or the compiler itself. There is no owner or admin, so once the contract is deployed no
address has any power over it. The only trust boundary that matters is the treasury address that
receives the whole supply.
