CB-181,,M-02 Investors cannot recover an unresolved order without the issuer,QuillAudits__Tradevu_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,tradevu,2026-09-30,no,no,2026-11,Medium,"Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
M-02
Investors cannot recover an unresolved order without
the issuer
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Function Name
rejectOrder(), resolveOrder()
Description
A placed order sits in orderPool until the issuer resolves or rejects it but only a holder of ISSUE_ROLE
on that token can do either.
resolveOrder also stops at maturity ( if (block.timestamp > maturityDate) revert
OfferingEnded(); ), so after maturity the only way out of an unresolved order is the issuer calling
rejectOrder , which has no deadline but needs the role. The token's DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE can revoke
the issuer's role, and then resolveOrder , rejectOrder , depositUSDC and withdrawRemainingUSDC are
uncallable for that offering until the admin grants the role again. The same lock applies if the issuer
loses its key or simply stops responding. withdrawRemainingUSDC only sweeps settlementPool , so the
money in orderPool is not swept either. It stays in the escrow.
```solidity
bytes32 ISSUE_ROLE = keccak256(""escrow.issuer.tradevu"");
if (!AccessControlUpgradeable(order.token).hasRole(ISSUE_ROLE, msg.sender)) {
    revert AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount(msg.sender, ISSUE_ROLE);
}
Impact
High
Each affected investor's principal plus fee stays locked with no on-chain recourse. Per order that is up to
maxInvestment plus the fee; across an offering, up to the whole orderPool . The investor receives
nothing: no tokens, no refund. The README documents the issuer's role in settlement, but not the case
where the issuer is absent.
Likelihood
Low
Low. It needs an unresponsive or removed issuer, a lost key, or an admin revoking the role. Because the
loss is permanent for the investor, it is worth removing the dependency.
