Medium Severity Issues
Medium Severity Issues
M-03
One blacklisted investor blocks the issuer's whole
refund batch
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow
Function Name
rejectOrder(), resolveOrder()
Description
rejectOrder and resolveOrder process up to 100 orders in one transaction and pay each recipient directly
inside the loop: the refund to the investor in rejectOrder (L260), and the principal to the calling issuer in
resolveOrder (L368). USDC reverts any transfer to or from a blacklisted address.
If one investor in a refund batch is blacklisted, their transfer reverts, and so does the whole transaction:
nobody in the batch is refunded. A blacklisted issuer address cannot resolve any order, because the
principal is always paid to the caller. A USDC-wide pause stops every flow at once.
The issuer has to identify the failing order and resubmit the batch without it. The blacklisted investor's
own order cannot be refunded until the blacklisting is lifted.
Impact
Medium
Low. Other investors' refunds and settlements are delayed until the issuer rebuilds the batch, but no
funds are lost. The blacklisted investor's funds stay in the escrow, though USDC would freeze them
anyway.
Likelihood
Medium
Low. Requires USDC's issuer to blacklist a participant.
