Path
Renouncing ownership freezes the shared token logic
Description
Every TokenProxy reads its logic address from one shared ImplementationAuthority and only the
owner can change it.
Ownable exposes renounceOwnership() which sets the owner to the zero address. After that no one
can call updateImplementation , and the logic every token resolves to is frozen.
Ownership can also be lost by a transfer to a wrong address, because transferOwnership takes effect
immediately.
```solidity
contract ImplementationAuthority is IImplementationAuthority, Ownable {
    function updateImplementation(address _newImplementation) external onlyOwner { ... }
}
Impact
Medium
A bug found later in the token logic cannot be fixed through the authority. Funds are not at risk from the
renounce itself, and a token that is working keeps working.
Likelihood
Low
Recommendation
1. Keep the owner as a multisig behind a timelock.
2. If the logic is meant to stay upgradeable, disable the renounce and use a two-step transfer:
[...excerpt ends]"
