Acknowledged
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Function Name
placeOrder(), resolveOrder()
Description
placeOrder checks the cap against minted supply only.
Tokens are minted only at resolveOrder , so totalSupply() does not move while orders are pending.
Any number of orders can be accepted whose combined tokens exceed the cap. In a live test, two 1,500
USDC orders (300 tokens each, cap 400) were both accepted. resolveOrder repeats the cap check
inside its loop, so the first order that would pass the cap reverts the entire batch.
```solidity
uint256 currentTotalSupply = IERC20(token).totalSupply();
if (currentTotalSupply + tokensToMint > maxTotalSupply) {
    ...
    revert TotalSupplyExceeded(tokensToMint, availableTokens);
}
Impact
Low
Orders beyond the cap hold investor funds in orderPool until the issuer rejects them. One unfillable ID
in a batch of up to 100 blocks the other 99 until the issuer finds and removes it. No funds are lost; the
cost is delay, extra issuer work and confusion.
Likelihood
Medium
edium. Any popular offering that approaches its cap hits this, and no attacker is needed.
Recommendation
Count tokens that are accepted but not yet minted, and release them on resolve and reject:
mapping(address => uint256) public pendingTokens;
// placeOrder
