Tradevu - Audit Report
Low Severity Issues
Low Severity Issues
L-07
A fully drained offering can never be marked settled
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Function Name
withdrawRemainingUSDC()
Description
withdrawRemainingUSDC sets isWithdrawn, zeroes the pool, and then reverts with NoUSDCLeft if there
was nothing to send, which undoes the flag. Once a pool has been paid out completely (after a capped
redemption as in issue 6, or with a 100% distribution fee), the sweep can never succeed and isWithdrawn
stays false for good. The README says the sweep ""marks the offering settled"".
Impact
Low
Low. No funds are involved, but the offering can never be closed on-chain. Monitoring and back-office
systems that wait for isWithdrawn or RemainingUSDCWithdrawn see it as unsettled indefinitely, and
every sweep attempt reverts with an error that reads like a fault.
Likelihood
Medium
Medium. Happens whenever redemptions drain the pool completely.
Recommendation
Allow an offering whose pool is empty to be closed (marked settled without a transfer), so the
documented end state is always reachable.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Applied the recommended fix.
34
www.quillaudits.com

Tradevu - Audit Report
Low Severity Issues
Low Severity Issues
L-08
getUserRedemptionAmount quotes payouts that will
not be made
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Function Name
getUserRedemptionAmount()
Description
getUserRedemptionAmount computes a holder's share and fee but ignores the pool balance, the claim
window and whether the offering has been swept. It keeps quoting the full payout after the window has
closed and the pool has been swept, when redemption can only revert. When the pool is short (issue 6),
it quotes more than redeemBillTokens pays. Before funding it returns 0, which is indistinguishable from
""nothing owed"".
Impact
Low
Low. Front ends and integrations that rely on the quote show holders amounts they cannot receive.
Likelihood
Medium
Recommendation
Make the quote reflect what redemption would actually pay at that moment, including the pool balance,
the claim window and settlement state, or document clearly that it is only an upper bound.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
