L-11
A cancelled order makes the issuer's reject batch revert
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Function Name
rejectOrder(), cancelOrder()
Description
In the fix review at commit ( b74b0ae ), we noted that the new function
cancelOrder marks the order resolved meanwhile rejectOrder in a batch loop reverts on a resolved
order:
// cancelOrder
order.resolved = true;
// rejectOrder, inside the batch loop
if (order.resolved) revert OrderAlreadyResolved();
An investor can cancel once maturityDate + CANCEL_GRACE has passed. If the issuer's batch of up to
100 IDs includes an order the investor cancels first, the whole batch reverts.
Impact
The issuer has to find the cancelled ID and resubmit without it. Other investors' refunds are delayed until
then. No funds are lost, and the investor who cancelled gets their money back.
Likelihood
Medium
Medium once the grace period has passed with unresolved orders; low before.
POC
1. Two investors place 500 USDC orders an and b. Time moves past maturity plus 7 days.
2. The investor of a calls cancelOrder(""a"").
3. The issuer calls rejectOrder([""a"",""b""]). It reverts with OrderAlreadyResolved.
4. The issuer calls rejectOrder([""b""]). It succeeds.
38
www.quillaudits.com

Tradevu - Audit Report
Low Severity Issues
L-11
A cancelled order makes the issuer's reject batch revert 
Recommendation
Use the order's own amount as the marker, with no new variable. cancelOrder already holds the amount
in a local, so it zeroes the stored one after setting the resolved flag, and rejectOrder skips an order that
is resolved and has zero amount:
// cancelOrder, after order.resolved = true;
order.amount = 0;
// rejectOrder, replacing the OrderAlreadyResolved revert in the loop
if (order.resolved) {
    if (order.amount == 0) continue;   // cancelled by its owner: nothing left to refund
    revert OrderAlreadyResolved();
}
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
(continued)
