Tradevu - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-02
The published interface does not match the escrow
Resolved
Path
ITradevuEscrow.sol, IToken.sol, TradevuEscrow.sol
Description
ITradevuEscrow.OrderDetails lists user before token and adds an orderRedeemed flag. getOrder, however,
returns (token, user, amount, resolved), and no redeemed flag exists anywhere. Both fields are
addresses, so a consumer that decodes getOrder using the interface struct's field order silently swaps
them.
The interfaces also declare errors that are never used. On the escrow: OrderAlreadyRedeemed,
UserAmountMismatch and MoreThanMaxPerUser. On the token: NotTransferrable,
DiscountBillAmountOvershoot and MoreThanMaxPerUser. They describe behaviour the contracts do not
have: per-order redemption tracking, a per-investor cap and non-transferable tokens. A repeated
redemption, for example, reverts with ZeroAmount rather than OrderAlreadyRedeemed.
Recommendation
Keep the interfaces in step with the implementation, and remove declarations for behaviour that is not
implemented.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
41
www.quillaudits.com

Tradevu - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-03
depositUSDC reports misleading errors
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Description
Two cases:
Unknown offering. For an offeringId that does not exist, depositUSDC calls getAmountsAndDate() on the
zero address before its zero-address check, so it reverts without a reason instead of with
UnsupportedToken. Every other entry point performs the check first.
Nothing minted. For an offering where orders were placed but none was resolved, the required deposit is
0. depositUSDC rejects 0 with ZeroAmount and any other amount with ""Insufficient deposit"", so the
offering can never be funded or closed, and withdrawRemainingUSDC reverts with DepositNotDone.
Pending orders can still be refunded by the issuer.
Recommendation
Validate the offering before making any external call, and handle offerings with nothing minted explicitly
so they can be closed cleanly.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
