Tradevu - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-05
Events misreport amounts and parties
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol, ITradevuEscrow.sol
Description
OrderPlaced and OrderRejected report the principal only, while the investor pays, or is refunded, the
principal plus the investment fee.
OrderResolved uses the same amount field for the number of bill tokens minted, while its sibling events
use USDC.
The investment fee sent to adminWallet in resolveOrder emits nothing; InvestmentFeeDeducted is
declared but never emitted.
DistributionFeeDeducted is emitted only when the fee is non-zero, while OrderRedeemed is emitted even
when nothing is paid.
USDCDeposited always records the escrow itself as receiver, and the depositing issuer is not recorded
anywhere.
actionID and offeringId are not indexed, so logs cannot be filtered by order or offering.
Recommendation
Have events report the full amounts actually moved, in consistent units, emit an event for every fee
transfer, and record the parties that actually act.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
