CB-196,,I-03 depositUSDC reports misleading errors,QuillAudits__Tradevu_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,tradevu,2026-09-30,no,no,2026-11,Informational,"Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-03
depositUSDC reports misleading errors
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol
Description
Two cases:
Unknown offering. For an offeringId that does not exist, depositUSDC calls getAmountsAndDate() on the
zero address before its zero-address check, so it reverts without a reason instead of with
UnsupportedToken. Every other entry point performs the check first.
Nothing minted. For an offering where orders were placed but none was resolved, the required deposit is
0. depositUSDC rejects 0 with ZeroAmount and any other amount with ""Insufficient deposit"", so the
offering can never be funded or closed, and withdrawRemainingUSDC reverts with DepositNotDone.
Pending orders can still be refunded by the issuer.
Recommendation
Validate the offering before making any external call, and handle offerings with nothing minted explicitly
so they can be closed cleanly.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
42
www.quillaudits.com

Tradevu - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-04
README says the whole balance is burned on
redemption
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow
Description
The README says that on redemption ""their whole balance is burned"". When the pool cannot cover a
holder's full payout, the code burns only the portion that was paid and leaves the rest in the holder's
wallet (see issue 6). Those leftover tokens cannot be redeemed for anything, because the pool is empty.
Recommendation
Align the documentation with the partial-burn behaviour, or change the behaviour to match the
documentation.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed
43
www.quillaudits.com

Tradevu - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-05
Events misreport amounts and parties
Resolved
Path
TradevuEscrow.sol, ITradevuEscrow.sol
Description
OrderPlaced and OrderRejected report the principal only, while the investor pays, or is refunded, the
principal plus the investment fee.
OrderResolved uses the same amount field for the number of bill tokens minted, while its sibling events
use USDC.
The investment fee sent to adminWallet in resolveOrder emits nothing; InvestmentFeeDeducted is
declared but never emitted.
DistributionFeeDeducted is emitted only when the fee is non-zero, while OrderRedeemed is emitted even
when nothing is paid.
USDCDeposited always records the escrow itself as receiver, and the depositing issuer is not recorded
anywhere.
actionID and offeringId are not indexed, so logs cannot be filtered by order or offering.
Recommendation
Have events report the full amounts actually moved, in consistent units, emit an event for every fee
transfer, and record the parties that actually act.
Tradevu Team's Comment
Fixed.
