CB-199,,H-01 ICV lender's fund will be locked if token for borrow is pulled from their wallet.,QuillAudits__Zynk_EVM_Atmos_Smart_Contract_Audit_Report_-_QuillAudits.pdf,QuillAudits,zynk,2026-10-22,no,yes,2026-11,High,"High Severity Issues
High Severity Issues
H-01
ICV lender's fund will be locked if token for borrow is
pulled from their wallet.
Resolved
Path
LibOrbitTransactions.sol
Function Name
borrow(), claim()
Description
When ICV lender's fund is used to borrow directly from their wallet i.e when user's wallet is used as
BorrowOperation.source the fund does not deposited into custody vault, instead it directly pulled from
the wallet and deposited into ZOV. After repaying when this fund comes back to custody vault at that
time this fund could lock in the vault permanently.
Assume a scenario:
1. UserA deposited 100k into custody vault, user.principalIn = 100k, user.principalOut = 0,
custodyBalance = 100k. net principal = 100 - 0 = 100k
2. 1st borrow operation: value = 100K. custody used as source. So custodyBalance = 0
3. 2nd borrow operation: value = 50k, ICV's wallet as source, user.principalIn = 100k, user.principalOut = 0,
custodyBalance = 0. net principal = 100 - 0 = 100k
4. Both loan repaid. Custody vault's balance = 150k.
5. cliff passed, user claimed. In claim() net = (principalIn - principalOut) = (100k - 0) = 100k. i.e claimable =
100k. But liquid = 150k. As liquid > claimable so liquid = claimable = 100k. As liquid != 0 so totalPaid =
liquid = 100k & 100k is transferred to the ICV user's wallet. As totalPaid == claimable so the loop will not
run. user.principalOut = 100k. Now net = 0.
6. At this point of time custody vault's balance = 50k. User can't claim again as net == 0.
Currently there is no such functionality in these contracts which will let the admins to move the fund
out. They can directly pay the user from outside of the contract but the amount will stay locked in the
custody vault.
The whole design is affected as there is no funtionality to pull tokens from userCustody vault in 
emergency.
Impact
ICV user's fund will be locked in custody vault. They cannot claim it even it was repaid by partners.
15
www.quillaudits.com

Zynk EVM - Audit Report
High Severity Issues
H-01
ICV lender's fund will be locked if token for borrow is pulled from
their wallet. 
Recommendation
Book external funding as principal at borrow time.
Zynk EVM Team's Comment
Borrowing is now restricted to funds already held in the borrowing ICV’s UserCustody vault. For every
position, the contract verifies that BorrowOperation.source matches that user’s derived custody-
vault address, rejects other sources before transferring funds, and transfers only from the custody
vault to the ZOV. The external-wallet pullToken path has been removed from borrow.
As a result, ICV funds must enter custody through the normal deposit or pledge flow before they can
be borrowed, keeping borrowed positions and repayment funds aligned with custody-based
accounting. LP users remain rejected by both borrow and repay.
(continued)
16
www.quillaudits.com

