High Severity Issues
H-03
Hardcoded `maxFee = 0` breaks fee-bearing CCTP
transfers
Resolved
Path
TransactionsFacet.sol
Function Name
deposit()
Description
[ TransactionsFacet.deposit() ](src/facets/TransactionsFacet.sol#L272-L283) always passes maxFee
= 0 to CCTP, while the configured minFinalityThreshold may request a Fast transfer ( 1000 ). maxFee
is the maximum part of the bridged amount that Circle may charge. Zynk has no normal configuration
path to raise this value.
If Circle applies a non-zero fee, a newer source messenger can reject the burn with Insufficient max
fee . On the older Ethereum mainnet messenger, the source burn can succeed. However, Circle's Solana
V2 destination program rejects the delivered message when fee_executed > max_fee ([fee check]
(https://github.com/circlefin/solana-cctp-
contracts/blob/b37d577fc1dc317ce9bc0316c5063afe38744ce3/programs/v2/token-messenger-minter-
v2/src/token_messenger_v2/instructions/handle_receive_finalized_message.rs#L176-L179)).
Zynk hardcodes maxFee = 0 , so it cannot pay any CCTP transfer fee. As a result, Fast transfers cannot
be reliably requested: Circle may degrade them to Standard transfers, removing the intended fast-
settlement property ([Circle CCTP fee documentation]
(https://developers.circle.com/cctp/concepts/fees#fee-tables)), or a fee-enforcing source deployment
may revert the deposit. Zynk has no normal governance/configuration path to update the fee cap as
Circle's fee policy changes.
if (!profile.chainBound) {
            ProtocolTypes.SolanaSettlementConfig storage config = 
LibCCTP.requireSolanaSettlement();
            if (mint != config.usdc) revert ZynkErrors.InvalidTokenMint();
            IZynkVault(vault)
                .burnCctp(
                    LibCCTP.requireMessenger(),
                    mint,
                    amount,
                    config.destinationDomain,
                    profile.solanaMintRecipient,
                    config.destinationCaller,
