POC
1. Zynk is configured with minFinalityThreshold = 1000 (Fast transfer). A user deposits 1,000 USDC .
2. deposit() transfers the USDC into the user's Solana custody vault, then calls CCTP with maxFee =
0 ([hard-coded argument](src/facets/TransactionsFacet.sol#L280)).
3. On the current older Ethereum messenger, Circle accepts the source burn. The vault is emptied,
Ethereum USDC is burned, and Zynk increases principalIn by 1,000 USDC ([accounting update]
(src/facets/TransactionsFacet.sol#L298)).
4. Assume Circle attests the Fast transfer with fee_executed = 0.1 USDC ( 100,000 USDC base units).
The delivered message contains max_fee = 0 and fee_executed = 100,000 .
5. The Solana CCTP V2 program evaluates 100,000 <= 0 and fails with [ FeeExceedsMaxFee ]
(https://github.com/circlefin/solana-cctp-
contracts/blob/b37d577fc1dc317ce9bc0316c5063afe38744ce3/programs/v2/token-messenger-minter-
v2/src/token_messenger_v2/instructions/handle_receive_finalized_message.rs#L178). The recipient
transfer happens only after that check ([transfer path](https://github.com/circlefin/solana-cctp-
contracts/blob/b37d577fc1dc317ce9bc0316c5063afe38744ce3/programs/v2/token-messenger-minter-
v2/src/token_messenger_v2/instructions/handle_receive_finalized_message.rs#L188-L209)), so it
transfers nothing to Zynk's configured Solana recipient. The finalized Ethereum burn cannot be undone
by that later Solana transaction failure.
Recommendation
Make maxFee and minFinalityThreshold governable configuration values with sensible bounds. Before
initiating a fee-bearing transfer, query Circle's applicable minimum/quoted fee and pass a maxFee that
covers it ([Circle CCTP fee documentation]
(https://developers.circle.com/cctp/concepts/fees#maximum-fee-parameter)). If no fee is acceptable,
restrict the route to a verified fee-free Standard-transfer configuration and document that operational
dependency.
