Zynk EVM - Audit Report
High Severity Issues
H-03
Hardcoded `maxFee = 0` breaks fee-bearing CCTP transfers
Zynk EVM Team's Comment
The deposit flow now supports per-transaction CCTP finality and fee-budget selection. The existing
deposit(bytes32,address,address,uint64) selector is preserved as a Standard, zero-fee-budget path.
The new depositWithCctpOptions(...) accepts a CctpSpeed enum and a caller-authorized feeBudget;
it maps Standard and Fast to Circle’s 2000 and 1000 thresholds, respectively. Unsupported modes
are rejected, and chain-bound deposits cannot use non-default CCTP options.
For Solana deposits, the contract pulls and burns principalAmount + feeBudget, forwards feeBudget
as CCTP’s maxFee, and credits only principalAmount to user principal. Checked arithmetic and the
existing transaction rollback protect source-side funds and accounting if the burn fails. The legacy
route-level finality field remains for compatibility, but new deposits choose their mode per call.
The contract does not fetch or calculate a live Circle fee quote; callers must obtain fee information
off-chain and supply an acceptable budget. If Circle charges less than that budget, the difference
remains in the destination mint amount, so destination-side surplus reconciliation is still an
operational consideration.
Updated commit
