Zynk EVM - Audit Report
Low Severity Issues
L-01
Emitted event arguments do not match stored state. 
1. The manager calls createOrder() with amount = 0 , metaPresent = true , and metadata {
""txAmount"": ""10000000000"" } to book a payout that was executed off-chain.
2. No tokens move. _metaAmount parses the string and order.amountOut is stored as 10,000 USDC.
3. OrderCreated is emitted with amount = 0 . An indexer records an order with no receivable until the
first OrderReplenished event arrives with a nonzero amount, at which point the order appears over-
repaid.
Recommendation
1. In LibOrbitTransactions.borrow() , pass operation.amount to _emitTx instead of amount , so
each TxEvent(""Borrow"") reports the slice taken from that user and matches the stored Position.
amountBorrowed .
2. In LibOrderActions.create() , pass effectiveAmount to emitOrderCreated instead of params.
amount , so OrderCreated reports the same value written to order.amountOut on the metadata path.
Zynk EVM Team's Comment
Fixed
