Zynk EVM - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-01
Missing wallet check may lead to loss of fund if wallet
is compromised
Resolved
Path
TransactionFacet.sol
Function Name
approveWithdraw()
Description
While approving a withdraw request ( TransactionFacet::approveWithdraw() ) it is not checked that the
destination wallet is one of approved wallet. If somehow the wallet used in withdraw request
compromised & an wallet update is done just before approving the withdraw request then the fund will
go to the compromised wallet
Impact
Loss of fund.
Recommendation
In approveWithdraw() it should be checked that request.destination must be one of 3 wallets.
Zynk EVM Team's Comment
Fixed
25
www.quillaudits.com

Zynk EVM - Audit Report
Informational Severity Issues
Informational Severity Issues
I-02
A compromised wallet's current owner can revoke a
wallet update everytime
Resolved
Path
UserOperationsFacet.sol
Function Name
rejectWalletUpdate()
Description
The UserOperationsFacet::rejectWalletUpdate() can be invoked by any of 3 wallets of users with admin.
But it is unnecessary & it can lead issue if any of 3 wallet is compromised. Assume one wallet was
comprimised, so when requestWalletUpdate() will be called the current owner of that compromised
wallet can revoke the wallet update request by calling rejectWalletUpdate(). As a result wallets can never
be updated.
Impact
Wallets can never be updated.
Recommendation
Make it only admin controlled function.
Zynk EVM Team's Comment
This is a non-negotiable requirement imposed by the LPs: the authority to reject a wallet update
request must not rest solely with the admin.
For such cases, we can explore alternative measures, including more definitive administrative
actions, where necessary.
Ignore the previous comment.
We are going with the recommended fix:
