Issue L-4: requestRedeem(0) spender check is redun-
dant cyclical-WM logic [RESOLVED]
Source: https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-09-maple-sept-7th-2026/issues/53
Summary
V500 MaplePoolManager.requestRedeem still special-cases shares_ == 0 so any spender
with a nonzero pool allowance can call requestRedeem(0, owner). On a cyclical
withdrawal manager, addShares(0, owner) postpones that owner’s entire lockedShares
balance. V500 pools use the queue WM, so the branch is dead leftover code.
Vulnerability Detail
The pool forwards the owner’s redeem request to the pool manager without reducing
allowance when the share amount is zero:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-09-maple-sept-7th-2026/blob/main/maple-la
bs__pool-v2-private/contracts/MaplePool.sol#L235-L248
if (msg.sender != owner_) {
_decreaseAllowance(owner_, msg.sender, escrowShares_);
}
// ...
IPoolManagerLike(manager).requestRedeem(escrowShares_, owner_, msg.sender);
The pool manager then only requires a nonzero allowance for the zero-share case, and
still calls addShares:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-09-maple-sept-7th-2026/blob/main/maple-la
bs__pool-v2-private/contracts/MaplePoolManager.sol#L336-L348
function requestRedeem(uint256 shares_, address owner_, address sender_) external
override whenNotPaused nonReentrant onlyPool {
,→
address pool_ = pool;
require(ERC20Helper.approve(pool_, withdrawalManager, shares_),
""PM:RR:APPROVE_FAIL"");
,→
if (sender_ != owner_ && shares_ == 0) {
require(IPoolLike(pool_).allowance(owner_, sender_) > 0,
""PM:RR:NO_ALLOWANCE"");
,→
}
IWithdrawalManagerLike(withdrawalManager).addShares(shares_, owner_);
13

emit RedeemRequested(owner_, shares_);
}
On a cyclical withdrawal manager, addShares(0, owner) moves that owner’s existing
locked shares to currentCycle + 2. A spender who was approved for any amount could
postpone the owner’s locked exit without consuming allowance. V500 setWithdrawalMan
ager only accepts a queue WM factory. The four upgraded pools (syrup USDC, syrup
USDT, syrup USDG, secured lending USDC) all use FIFO queue WMs. Queue addShares(0)
doesn't postpone locked shares, so the branch has no effect on in-scope upgraded pools.
Impact
Any spender with a leftover nonzero allowance can call requestRedeem(0, owner)
without consuming that allowance. The Pool Manager still forwards addShares(0, owner)
to the withdrawal manager. On a cyclical withdrawal manager that call postpones the
owner’s entire lockedShares balance to currentCycle + 2. The owner misses their current
exit window and waits two extra cycles to withdraw. In this specific case, the spender
can't steal shares or assets, but they can delay an LP’s redemption indefinitely by
repeating the call whenever a new window opens.
Tool Used
Manual Review
Recommendation
Consider removing the leftover branch:
if (sender_ != owner_ && shares_ == 0) {
require(IPoolLike(pool_).allowance(owner_, sender_) > 0, ""PM:RR:NO_ALLOWANCE"");
}
Discussion
