Issue H-1: Registered-but-disabled collateral is dropped
by the config replay, freezing every position that
holds it [RESOLVED]
Source:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit2/2026-08-delpho-update-aug-27th-2026/issues/66
Summary
The migration replays the token registry by iterating getAllSupportedTokens(), which
filters on the per-token enabled flag. WHYPE and KHYPE are registered-but-disabled on
the live provider, so their TokenConfig is never carried to the new one.
DelphoOracle does not read enabled. It gates on decimals == 0 || priceFeed == address
(0), so both tokens price normally today and back live USDV debt. After the repoint their
config is gone, the oracle reverts, and every position holding either token becomes
unwithdrawable and unliquidatable.
Vulnerability Detail
BaseConfigProviderUpgrade._migrateAllConfig seeds from oldConfig.getAllSupportedTo
kens(). That getter filters on enabled, returning [USDT, USDC] on chain while getTokenCou
nt() returns 4. The token/oracle and deposit-limit loops iterate only that array and
contain the only addToken, setTokenPriceBounds and setTokenStalenessAge call sites in
the prod upgrade tree. WHYPE and KHYPE are therefore never registered on the new
provider.
The oracle never agreed to that reading of enabled:
if (tokenConfig.decimals == 0 || tokenConfig.priceFeed == address(0)) revert
DO_UNSUPPORTED_TOKEN();
,→
Valuation also ignores the provider registry. VaultMath._getUserCollateralTokensAndAmo
unts builds its token array from depositedTokens[user], the Vault's own set, which is
cleared only when a balance reaches zero. Nothing removes a token from it on
deregistration. So the Vault still treats WHYPE as collateral while the provider no longer
has the feed to price it.
Verified against mainnet: getTokenConfig(WHYPE) returns (0x2b25BC41…, false, 18, 18),
oracle.getTokenPrice(WHYPE) returns 84244695, and an unregistered token reverts 0x7438
7a2d, which is DO_UNSUPPORTED_TOKEN(). The repointed stable Vault holds totalCollateral
(WHYPE) = 2166000000000000000. Two affected holders, both with live debt and both in the
sorted-debt list:
5

Address
