Impact
requestWithdrawal, claimWithdrawal, cancelWithdrawalRequest, collateralDeposit, mintS
table and liquidation all revert for affected addresses. Only repayStable still works. _val
idateUserLTV prices before checking debt, so debt-free depositors are frozen too, and
LTV covers the whole position, so unaffected collateral is trapped alongside it.
Positions become unliquidatable, converting any HYPE drawdown into protocol bad
debt. USDV fallback redemption also reverts for every redeemer, because it calls getUser
CollateralDetails per borrower with no error handling and both holders are in the list it
iterates.
The failure is deterministic and occurs the moment the Vault is repointed. isTokenSuppor
ted(WHYPE) returns false before and after, so the divergence is invisible to an operator
checking that getter.
