terfaces/IDelphoOracleConfig.sol#L22
Tool Used
Manual Review.
Recommendation
Price both PSM legs through the oracle and clamp each direction so it favours the
protocol:
11

• Mint: use min(oraclePrice, 1e6). Depegged collateral mints proportionally less
USDV, and a premium above par never mints more than par. This needs no new
configuration, because getTokenPriceStrict already returns exactly this for USDC
given the live tokenPriceBounds(USDC) of (1000000, true).
• Redeem: use max(oraclePrice, 1e6). A redeemer never receives more collateral
units than par during a depeg, and never receives premium collateral cheaply. This
requires a floor, so add a minPrice field to TokenPriceBounds or apply the bound in
the PSM.
Consider also pausing psmMint automatically when the oracle price deviates beyond a
configured threshold, using the existing per-collateral psmMintPaused mapping. Note that
routing through getTokenPriceStrict also inherits its staleness revert, which is the
desired behaviour: the PSM should not mint against an unknown price.
