Issue M-3: PSM min single redemption strands dust
[RESOLVED]
Source:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit2/2026-08-delpho-update-aug-27th-2026/issues/74
Summary
DelphoPSM::redeem() enforces a floor on the size of a single redemption but never checks
the residual the redemption leaves behind, so any redemption that drops globalBufferFu
nds[collateral] (or psmLiabilities[collateral]) to a nonzero value below psmMinSingle
Redemption strands that residual permanently and bricks the entire PSM redemption path
for that collateral until an admin reallocates funds or new collateral is minted in.
Vulnerability Detail
DelphoPSM::redeem() rejects anything smaller than the configured floor before doing any
other work: DelphoPSM.sol#L195.
A valid redemption therefore has to satisfy psmMinSingleRedemption <= usdvAmount <= m
in(psmLiabilities[collateral], globalBufferFunds[collateral]). Nothing in the
function constrains what the subtraction leaves behind, and no code path anywhere in
the contract exempts a final sweep from the floor. The moment min(psmLiabilities[col
lateral], globalBufferFunds[collateral]) lands strictly between zero and psmMinSingl
eRedemption, the feasible interval is empty and every possible redemption reverts: a large
enough amount fails the balance checks with DPSM_INSUFFICIENT_LIQUID_RESERVE or DPSM
_INSUFFICIENT_LIABILITIES, and a small enough amount fails the floor with DPSM_REDEMPT
ION_BELOW_MIN.
Impact
The redemption side of the peg stability module can be shut down for a collateral by a
single ordinary looking redemption, removing the peg floor for every USDV holder until
an admin intervenes. Residual collateral below psmMinSingleRedemption in the buffer
book is unredeemable through the PSM entirely. The griefing cost is only the redeem fee
on the attacker's own redemption, and the state is trivially re established after each
recovery, so the denial of service is cheap and repeatable.
Code Snippet
DelphoPSM.sol#L193-L197 and DelphoPSM.sol#L220-L234
if (usdvAmount == 0) revert DPSM_ZERO_AMOUNT();
13

if (usdvAmount < psmMinSingleRedemption) revert DPSM_REDEMPTION_BELOW_MIN();
if (usdvAmount > psmMaxSingleRedemption) revert DPSM_REDEMPTION_ABOVE_MAX();
[...excerpt ends]"
