Issue L-1: A system address must never be config-
ured for USDC, because both plausible values silently
destroy funds [RESOLVED]
Source:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit2/2026-08-delpho-update-aug-27th-2026/issues/69
Summary
USDC has no HyperCore system-address bridge route. Its only valid path to Core is coreD
epositWalletUsdc().deposit(amount, destinationDex), and DelphoBaseExecutor._transf
erCollateralToCore correctly routes it through a dedicated branch that never reads syst
emAddress.
The generic else branch protects against a mis-route with if (systemAddress == addres
s(0)) revert DEB_INVALID_SYSTEM_ADDRESS(). Configuring any value for USDC disarms
that guard, and both plausible values destroy funds: the initializer hardcodes the
deposit-wallet contract, and the live provider holds a codeless address.
Vulnerability Detail
The repo's own vendored HyperEVM library is explicit. CoreWriterLib.bridgeToCore
computes getSystemAddress(token) and then deliberately refuses to use it for USDC:
if (HLConstants.isUsdc(token)) {
IERC20(HLConstants.usdc()).approve(address(coreDepositWallet), evmAmount);
coreDepositWallet.deposit(evmAmount, uint32(type(uint32).max));
} else if (isHype(token)) { ... } else {
IERC20(tokenAddress).safeTransfer(systemAddress, evmAmount);
}
PrecompileLib.getTokenIndex also short-circuits USDC before consulting the token
registry, indicating USDC is not a registry-linked token with an EVM system-address
route.
Both configurable values are unsafe as a safeTransfer destination:
• 0x2000000000000000000000000000000000000000, the current live value, has zero
bytes of code. A transfer succeeds at the ERC-20 level, nothing credits a
HyperCore balance, and there is no owner or admin. Funds are permanently lost.
• 0x6B9E773128f453f5c2C60935Ee2DE2CBc5390A24, the initializer default, is the deposit
wallet itself: a transparent upgradeable proxy whose admin is not Delpho. A plain s
afeTransfer bumps its balance without invoking deposit(), so there is no Core
credit, no event and no attribution. The funds merge into its balance and recovery
requires Hyperliquid's cooperation.
15

The USDC branch is selected by else if (token == cfg.stablecoinToken(StableCoinTyp
e.USDC)). Anything that makes USDC miss that comparison, such as stablecoinToken(US
DC) being unset on a partially configured provider or pointed at a different address,
drops USDC into the generic branch, which then reads the configured system address
and sends there.
Note this is not migration-specific: the live provider already returns 0x20000000000000000
00000000000000000000000 for systemAddress(USDC), so the guard is disarmed in
production today.
Impact
The guard that exists to convert a USDC mis-route into a clean revert is disabled by
configuration.
