Issue L-6: PSM daily limit bypass via multiple wallets
[ACKNOWLEDGED]
Source:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit2/2026-08-delpho-update-aug-27th-2026/issues/75
This issue has been acknowledged by the team but won't be fixed at this time.
Summary
DelphoPSM::redeem() enforces its rolling redemption cap against the user address it is
handed, and that address is simply the externally owned account that called DelphoRout
er::psmRedeem(). Because creating a fresh account is free and permissionless, psmMaxDai
lyRedemption constrains nobody who is willing to split a redemption across several
addresses, and the only cap that actually binds is the global tumbling window.
Vulnerability Detail
The per user window is keyed on the user argument in two mappings, psmStartRedeemable
Timestamp[user][collateral] and psmDailyRedemptions[user][collateral], both
declared in DelphoPSM.
DelphoPSM::redeem() reads the accumulator for that address, adds the current amount
and compares it against psmMaxDailyRedemption, here. A caller who has never redeemed
has prevUserStart == 0, so userWindowUsed stays zero and the whole daily allowance is
available to them immediately.
The user value is not an attested identity. DelphoPSM::redeem() only requires that the
caller is the configured router, here, and DelphoRouter::psmRedeem() forwards its own msg.
sender straight through as user, here. So the key is nothing more than whichever address
funded and signed the transaction, and an actor holding USDV can distribute it to N
fresh addresses and obtain N times the intended per address allowance in the same
block.
Impact
The protection intended by psmMaxDailyRedemption does not exist against any
determined redeemer. A single actor can drain up to the full psmMaxGlobalDailyRedemptio
n and up to the whole globalBufferFunds[collateral] book within one window by
fanning out across addresses, exhausting the redemption buffer that honest users share
and forcing the remainder of the window to revert with DPSM_INSUFFICIENT_LIQUID_RESER
VE. Severity is Low because the global window and the buffer balance still bound the
total outflow, and no funds leave at an incorrect rate.
29

