Issue L-7: Redemption ignores per market health [AC-
KNOWLEDGED]
Source:
https://github.com/sherlock-audit2/2026-08-delpho-update-aug-27th-2026/issues/77
This issue has been acknowledged by the team but won't be fixed at this time.
Summary
DelphoRouterV2::redeem() resolves the target market purely from the caller supplied mar
ketKey, and each DelphoStableManager::redeem() instance can only see its own market,
so nothing steers redemption toward the weaker of the two markets that share the same
USDV liability. Redemption is health aware inside a market and completely health blind
between markets.
Vulnerability Detail
The multi market upgrade maps every collateral token to a market key and every market
key to its own DelphoConfigProvider, which in turn owns its own vault, stable manager
and sorted debt list (configureMarket). The production migration configures exactly two
of them, STABLE_MARKET backed by USDC and USDT and NON_STABLE_MARKET backed by
WHYPE and kHYPE, and wires the same DelphoStable token into both providers, so both
markets mint and burn the same USDV (migration wiring).
Inside a single market the redemption ordering is exactly right. DelphoStableManager::_r
edeemFromBorrowers() snapshots borrowers starting from IDelphoSortedDebts::getHead()
, and the list is maintained in ascending LCR order by DelphoStableManager::_updateSort
edDebt(), so the head is the borrower closest to insolvency and redemption pressure
lands on the weakest positions first (sorted debt walk, LCR ordering).
Between markets there is no such ordering, and no check of any kind. DelphoRouterV2::r
edeem() takes the market key from the caller and resolves it through DelphoRouterV2::_ma
rketByKey(), which only verifies that a provider has been registered for that key (redeem,
_marketByKey). The selected market's DelphoStableManager::redeem() then runs entirely
against its own state and its own config, and validates only that the caller is the router
(_validateCaller). It has no reference to the sibling market and no way to acquire one.
Every throttle that could have created balance is per instance as well. startRedeemableT
imestamp, dailyRedemptions, globalRedemptionWindowStart and globalDailyRedemptions
are all storage of one DelphoStableManager, and StableManagerLib::checkAndUpdateDaily
Window() charges them against that market's own RedemptionConfig
[...excerpt ends]"
