Recommendation
Pay the redeemer a bonus in collateral that scales with how far the market sits above its
target LTV, keep the debt reduction at the net redeemed amount so the accounting is
unchanged, and switch the bonus off near the liquidation threshold where handing out
extra collateral would itself push the market down. The seize budget and the debt credit
are already separate values in both redemption paths, so the change is local.
Apply the same treatment in DelphoStableManager::_redeemFromBorrowers() by widening
targetUsd in DelphoStableManager::_processOneFallbackBorrower() while still crediting
only usdApplied against the borrower's debt, and bound the bonus so that a single
redemption can never raise the market LTV.
