An operator extends the bridge to a new chain and runs the script unchanged; the 
deployment succeeds and reports no error. Days later, the team attempts to grant 
MINTER_ROLE and BURNER_ROLE to the newly deployed MintBurnOFTAdapter but 
cannot: scheduling that grant requires PROPOSER_ROLE, a role that the script assigned to 
an address where no account exists on this chain, and that no other account holds. The 
timelock is its own only administrator, so no transaction can add one. The token, its 
timelock, and their block explorer verifications must all be discarded and redeployed. 
