because the script will then refuse to run on any chain whose proposer has not been 
established, and will refuse to name a proposer that cannot originate transactions. 
Long term, grant CANCELLER_ROLE and PROPOSER_ROLE to different parties and provision 
an explicit recovery administrator for every timelock the repository deploys. This will 
prevent the issue because OpenZeppelin will grant each proposer CANCELLER_ROLE as 
well, so adding a second proposer alone will leave a lost or hostile first proposer able to 
cancel any repair. 
 
 
 
