CB-225,FR-380,Guard trigger will fail if latestConfirmed changes,Trail_of_Bits__2026-09-offchain-osp-guard-securityreview.pdf,Trail of Bits,arbitrum-bold,2026-08-12,no,yes,2026-09,Informational,"
Detailed Findings 
1. Guard trigger will fail if latestConfirmed changes 
Severity: Informational 
Difficulty: High 
Type: Data Validation 
Finding ID: TOB-OSPGUARD-1 
Target: src/challengeV2/guard/OspSoundnessGuard.sol 
 
Description 
Before pausing the rollup, the guard requires the caller to prove that the challenged fork is 
still live. _requireDescendantOfLatestConfirmed does this by walking the assertion 
chain upward from the fork point, and it requires the walk to end exactly on 
rollup.latestConfirmed(). 
function _requireDescendantOfLatestConfirmed( 
    bytes32 prevAssertionHash, 
    bytes32[] calldata checkpoints, 
    AssertionAncestryStep[] calldata ancestry 
) internal view { 
    bytes32 cursor = prevAssertionHash; 
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < checkpoints.length; i++) { 
        if (!provenDescendsFrom[cursor][checkpoints[i]]) { 
            revert AncestryLinkNotProven(cursor, checkpoints[i]); 
        } 
        cursor = checkpoints[i]; 
    } 
    bytes32 latestConfirmed = rollup.latestConfirmed(); 
    if (_walkUp(cursor, ancestry) != latestConfirmed) { 
        revert NotDescendantOfLatestConfirmed(prevAssertionHash, latestConfirmed); 
    } 
} 
Figure 1.1: The _requireDescendantOfLatestConfirmed function 
(OspSoundnessGuard.sol#L169–L185) 
The walk is fixed in the caller’s calldata, but latestConfirmed is read at execution time. 
While a challenge is open, latestConfirmed trails the fork point by every assertion 
created in the last confirmPeriodBlocks, and it advances each time one of those 
assertions is confirmed.  
Since minimumAssertionPeriod is 75 blocks, this occurs repeatedly over the life of a 
challenge, as a result of ordinary validator activity. ​
​
        Trail of Bits​
7​
Offchain Labs OSP Soundness Guard​
        PUBLIC​
​
Security Assessment 

​
If latestConfirmed advances before the transaction is executed, the walk passes through 
the new value and terminates on the previous one. The comparison then fails, and the 
transaction reverts.  
Recommendations 
Short term, document this scenario so that it does not cause confusion when triggered. It is 
unlikely to be triggered and requires only a new transaction to be sent to overcome it. 
 
 
 
​
        Trail of Bits​
