2. Scripts contain references to previous contract versions 
Severity: Informational 
Difficulty: High 
Type: Configuration 
Finding ID: TOB-OSPGUARD-2 
Target: scripts/deployOspSoundnessGuard.ts 
 
Description 
The OSP guard deployment script contains two identifiers left over from renaming Pauser 
to PauseExecutor. These leftover identifiers cause two failures. The first occurs before 
any contract is deployed, so the second failure is unreachable until the first is fixed.   
First, the script requests a nonexistent Pauser artifact instead of PauseExecutor (figure 
2.1). Therefore, Hardhat fails before deploying any contracts. 
const pauser = await deployContract( 
  'Pauser', 
  deployer, 
  [target.upgradeExecutor, target.upgradeExecutor, []], 
  true, 
  true 
) 
Figure 2.1: Deployment using a nonexistent contract artifact 
(deployOspSoundnessGuard.ts#L87–L97) 
Once the artifact name is corrected, the script reaches its call to guard.pauser(). The 
guard exposes the pause executor through the autogenerated pe() getter, so this call also 
fails. It occurs after deployment but before the script prints the governance calldata 
needed to install the guard. 
if ((await guard.pauser()).toLowerCase() !== pauser.address.toLowerCase()) { 
  throw new Error('guard points at a different pauser') 
} 
Figure 2.2: Sanity check using a nonexistent getter 
(deployOspSoundnessGuard.ts#L115–L122) 
Recommendations 
Short term, replace Pauser with PauseExecutor and guard.pauser() with 
guard.pe(). 
 
