rotation, decrypting the old ciphertext with the new key returns the 
ErrDecryptionFailed error (decryption). l2geth then leaves the queued 
relayMessage function call unchanged, so the L2ScrollMessenger contract forwards 
the finalizeDepositERC20Encrypted function call to the L2 gateway. The gateway does 
not implement this function, so the call reverts before minting. The messenger emits the 
FailedRelayedMessage event without marking the message as executed, while the relay 
transaction succeeds (gateway interface, relay handling). 
The replayMessage function requires a previously enqueued message hash, so the user 
cannot replace its ciphertext with one encrypted under the new key. Replays under that key 
follow the same failure path. 
