A user's deposit encrypted under K0 runs out of gas on L2. Before the user replays it with a 
higher gas limit, the key manager rotates to K1. The replay retains the K0 ciphertext but 
receives a K1 queue index, so authenticated decryption fails. l2geth includes the 
encrypted call unchanged; the gateway call fails before minting, while the outer transaction 
