Short term, make l2geth validate the complete 65-byte uncompressed public-key 
encoding, including the 0x04 prefix, and route invalid-ciphertext errors through the 
existing path that leaves the original L1 transaction unchanged. 
Long term, run shared ciphertext vectors through l2geth and the prover and require both 
paths to produce identical transaction bytes, including leaving invalid ciphertexts 
