an extra proposal type without making the Governor initialization revert. If the operator 
later clears that type instead of redeploying, a proposal created under it can pass with no 
votes and execute through the L1 Timelock. 
The configurator stores the proposal types that the L1 Governor uses to evaluate 
proposals. Each type defines a quorum, an approval threshold, a name, and an optional 
voting module. It is meant to be initialized once, by the Governor’s own initializer, and it 
treats a nonzero stored governor address as proof that initialization has already 
happened (figure 7.1). 
function initialize(address _governor, ProposalType[] calldata _proposalTypesInit) 
external { 
    if (address(governor) != address(0)) revert AlreadyInit(); 
    governor = IAgoraGovernor(_governor); 
    for (uint8 i = 0; i < _proposalTypesInit.length; i++) { 
        _setProposalType( 
            i, 
            _proposalTypesInit[i].quorum, 
            _proposalTypesInit[i].approvalThreshold, 
            _proposalTypesInit[i].name, 
            _proposalTypesInit[i].module 
        ); 
    } 
} 
