Description 
The SCR runner reports step 14 as blocked after a successful funding transaction until the 
transaction’s L1 block is finalized, because its escrow coverage check reads finalized state 
but is not marked as a check that can resolve with time. The operator therefore sees a 
failed-check status during normal finality lag, which can prompt an unnecessary halt. 
Step 14 mints the full 1B L1 SCR supply into the L1 gateway escrow. Its post-check runs the 
live invariants, including escrowCoversSupply, which confirms that the L1 escrow balance 
covers the L2 SCR supply. To avoid acting on state that a reorganization could undo, the 
function reads both balances at finalized blocks (figure 8.1). 
