Description 
When the USX canary claim’s relay transaction succeeds but the inner gateway call fails, the 
runner reports the canary step as waiting indefinitely and never sends another relay. A 
gateway fault therefore looks like a pending claim, and the final readiness gate cannot 
complete until the operator diagnoses it outside the runner. 
The canary claim step proves the bridge end to end by claiming a small USX withdrawal on 
Ethereum through one relayMessageWithProof transaction to the L1 messenger. If the 
gateway call fails, the messenger does not revert. It emits a FailedRelayedMessage event 
and leaves the message unexecuted, so the outer transaction succeeds and the message 
can be relayed again (figure 14.1). 
