Impact
Informational
Description
The PcfaBridge contract imports OpenZeppelin's upgradable proxy utilities alongside the
non-upgradable ReentrancyGuard module:
import {Initializable}
from ""@openzeppelin-contracts/proxy/utils/Initializable.sol"";
import {UUPSUpgradeable}
from ""@openzeppelin-contracts/proxy/utils/UUPSUpgradeable.sol"";
import {ReentrancyGuard}
from ""@openzeppelin-contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol"";
The ReentrancyGuard module from OpenZeppelin is not upgradable.
Impact
If storage slots change unexpectedly during a future upgrade, the reentrancy guard or other logic
sharing the same storage slot could break.
Recommendations
Use ReentrancyGuardTransient, which uses transient storage to reduce gas costs and avoids
consuming persistent storage slots for the reentrancy guard, making it well-suited to upgradeable
contracts.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Pacifica, and a fix was implemented in commit 2c3338d1 ↗.
