Impact
For voting round below the migration boundary that holds no root, the Relay can report a successful
verification for a zero leaf that no signing policy ever committed to, so the finalization guarantee the
interface documents does not hold on historical rounds.
The demonstrated bypass is limited to a zero leaf with an empty proof against a zero root. It does not
establish arbitrary nonzero leaf forgery. Consumers that derive their leaf as the hash of an encoded
payload are therefore unaffected in practice.
Recommendations
We recommend gating the delegated branch on the old relay's own finalization view before forward-
ing the proof, which mirrors the invariant the local branch enforces:
require(oldRelay.isFinalized(_protocolId, _votingRoundId), NotFinalized());
bool ok = oldRelay.verify(_protocolId, _votingRoundId, _leaf, _proof);
require(ok, OldRelayVerificationFailed());
