2.6.
Ownership transfers are not subject to the timelock
Target
Relay
Category
Business Logic
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
Relay inherits OwnableWithTimelock, which applies the configured delay only to functions using
the onlyOwnerWithTimelock modifier. However, OwnableWithTimelock inherits transferOwner-
ship from OpenZeppelin's OwnableUpgradeable without overriding it. The inherited implementa-
tion uses onlyOwner and updates ownership directly:
function transferOwnership(address newOwner) public virtual onlyOwner {
if (newOwner == address(0)) {
revert OwnableInvalidOwner(address(0));
}
_transferOwnership(newOwner);
}
Consequently, a successful call to transferOwnership takes effect immediately, even when time-
lockDurationSeconds is nonzero. Ownership transfers cannot be queued through the contract's
built-in timelock.
Impact
The configured timelock provides no review or cancellation window for ownership changes. An in-
correct transfer therefore takes effect immediately and cannot be canceled by the previous owner.
This is an informational limitation of the governance design: transfers remain restricted to the
owner, and the new owner remains subject to the configured delay for timelocked operations.
Recommendations
If ownership changes are intended to receive the same delay as other administrative operations,
override transferOwnership to use onlyOwnerWithTimelock.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Flare, and a fix was implemented in commit 8367d2d4 ↗.
Zellic © 2026
