For larger signer sets, mandating that the signatures be sorted by signer can
save gas
Target
Fdc2Verification
Category
Optimization
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
Thisdiffmodifiesthe verifyTeeSignaturesprocessbyaddinganextensionIDfield, andabstracting
out the verification function into a new _verifyTeeSignatures:
function _verifyTeeSignatures(
IFlareTeeManager _flareTeeManager,
uint256 _extensionId,
Signature[] calldata _signatures,
bytes32 _messageHash
)
internal view
returns (address[] memory _signingTeeIds)
{
_signingTeeIds = new address[](_signatures.length);
for (uint256 i = 0; i < _signatures.length; i++) {
address teeId = _verifyTeeSignature(_flareTeeManager, _extensionId,
_signatures[i], _messageHash);
for (uint256 j = 0; j < i; j++) {
require(_signingTeeIds[j] != teeId, DuplicatedTeeId(teeId));
}
_signingTeeIds[i] = teeId;
}
}
The implementation of this function is quadratic in the number of signatures, because each signa-
ture needs to be checked for duplicates against each other signature.
Impact
This check does not need to be quadratic in gas cost. If there are many signers, then considerable
gas can be saved by redesigning it.
Zellic © 2026
Page 18 of 26

Flare Relay Network Diff Smart Contract Patch Review
September 14, 2026
Recommendations
If the interface can be changed, then we recommend requiring that the signatures be sorted by
signer. This would easily make the signatures checkable in linear time, as each signature just needs
to be compared against the next.
Remediation
Flare has acknowledged this issue and provided the following comment:
Since any change would require off-chain components to adopt it, and we expect at most 3–5
TEE machines and 3–5 cosigners, we have decided to leave it as is.
