3.2.
OFT transport recipients can decode to zero after source principal is debited
Target
OFTCoreUpgradeable and Frax OFT implementations
ID
ZELLIC-4AVT21
Category
Integration Risks
Severity
Low
Likelihood
Low
Impact
Low
Description
The shared OFT source path debits the sender before encoding SendParam.to, but it does not
validate that the outer transport recipient is usable on the destination:
(uint256 amountSentLD, uint256 amountReceivedLD) = _debit(...);
(message, hasCompose) = OFTMsgCodec.encode(_sendParam.to, ...);
The destination truncates the wire value to an EVM address and passes it directly to _credit:
address toAddress = address(uint160(uint256(_message.sendTo())));
uint256 amountReceivedLD = _credit(toAddress, ...);
The reviewed minting implementations and adapters pass that address to _mint or an
underlying-token transfer. If it is zero, destination credit reverts after the source debit has finalized
in a separate transaction.
A recipient of bytes32(0) is only the canonical trigger. Any nonzero value whose low 160 bits are
zero, such as bytes32(uint256(1) << 160), also decodes to address(0). This path is directly
reachable through public OFT.send() without a hop.
Impact
An initiating sender can burn source OFT supply or lock adapter collateral without completing
delivery to a usable destination. The caller selects the recipient and funds the debit; no path was
found to alter another sender's recipient or debit a passive holder.
The outcome depends on the destination token. Where credit reaches an OpenZeppelin _mint,
the zero recipient reverts and the message stalls undelivered. The Ethereum sfrxUSD lockbox is
different: its inner token derives from Solmate through SfrxUSD to LinearRewardsErc4626_2,
which extends solmate/mixins/ERC4626.sol, and Solmate's ERC20.transfer credits the
destination without checking it against zero. Delivery to a zero recipient therefore succeeds there,
Zellic © 2026
←Back to Contents
Page 19 of 505

frxUSD Ecosystem Smart Contract Security Assessment
October 19, 2026
and the custodied balance becomes permanently unrecoverable at address(0) while
totalSupply is unchanged.
Redirecting zero credit to a sentinel such as address(0xdead) would complete the message but
make the loss irreversible rather than protect the sender.
Recommendations
Reject bytes32(0) in shared OFT quote and send logic. Before debit on an EVM route, also reject a
recipient for which address(uint160(uint256(sendParam.to))) == address(0).
Keep this check route-aware because the same bytes32 field supports non-EVM destinations. A
destination-side zero check is useful defense in depth, but the loss-prevention check must run on
the source before principal moves.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Frax, and fixes were implemented in the following commits:
• af76ecc1 ↗
• 5fb31cb2 ↗
