Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Frax, and a fix was implemented in commit 2e10f596 ↗.
Frax provided the following comment:
Refunds stay in LZD, a 1:1 claim on a whitelisted stablecoin; reverse-swapping a dust sur-
plus after the message is committed would re-introduce the DEX quote-versus-settlement
divergence the fee path pads against. Hop-held refunds are zero by construction: Remote-
HopV201Tempo and RemoteMintRedeemHopTempo quote and send in one transaction and
the OFT wraps exactly fee.nativeFee, so the endpoint's required fee equals the amount sup-
plied and nothing is refunded. There is no caller excess to attribute; swap headroom is already
returned to the payer in the fee token in the same call, and recoverERC20 only covers LZD
a third party leaves on the endpoint. For direct callers the refund denomination and recipi-
ent requirements will be documented on the public Tempo integration page (Fee Refunds), is
documented in the frax-oft-upgradeable README and the NatSpec: pass the freshest quote
unmodified, use a refund address that can transfer LZD or call unwrap, and redeem with un-
wrap(whitelistedToken, to, amount).
