3.4.
Unbounded minters_array growth can prevent minter removal
Target
FrxUSD
ID
ZELLIC-VTXKC7
Category
Code Maturity
Severity
Low
Likelihood
Low
Impact
Low
Description
The addMinter function appends every newly authorized minter to minters_array. The
removeMinter function clears authorization in the mapping, linearly scans the complete array, and
replaces the matching entry with an address(0) tombstone:
minters[minter_address] = true;
minters_array.push(minter_address);
for (uint256 i = 0; i < minters_array.length; i++) {
if (minters_array[i] == minter_address) {
minters_array[i] = address(0);
break;
}
}
Removed slots are never reused. Repeated add-and-remove cycles therefore increase the array
length and the worst-case scan cost for later entries. The minters mapping remains the
authoritative authorization state; the array contains zero-address tombstones.
Impact
Only the privileged timelock can grow the array, and the reviewed live length was 10, so there is no
immediate gas-limit failure. With sufficient historical growth, however, removing a compromised
late-index minter can exceed the block gas limit. The transaction then reverts, including the
mapping deletion, preventing revocation.
Recommendations
Use an address-to-index mapping with bounded deletion, or reuse tombstoned slots if stable
indexes are required. Also cap and monitor the array length, and retain a mapping-only
emergency revocation path whose cost does not depend on historical entries.
Document that minters is authoritative and zero array entries are tombstones.
