}
The policyExists modifier rejects only ID zero, while isFrozen assumes blacklist semantics. A
nonexistent, non-BLACKLIST, or incorrect-admin policy can make freeze/thaw revert or invert
isFrozen.
Impact
An authorized deployer can initialize either one-shot path with no local owner. The alternate path
can also bind an unusable policy, requiring a proxy upgrade or action by the actual policy
administrator to recover.
Reviewed production scripts use the normal initializer with a multi-signature owner. The issue
therefore requires a privileged deployment mistake, not an unprivileged call against an initialized
proxy.
Recommendations
Reject a zero owner in both initializers. For initializeWithPolicy, also reject policy ID zero and
require an existing BLACKLIST policy whose administrator is address(this).
