Initializers accept a zero owner, and initializeWithPolicy accepts unus-
able policies
Target
FrxUSDPolicyAdminTempo
ID
ZELLIC-2SEV54
Category
Coding Mistakes
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
Both initialization paths transfer ownership without rejecting address(0). The normal path still
creates a BLACKLIST policy administered by the proxy, but no local owner remains to manage
freezers, thaw accounts, or transfer policy administration.
The initializeWithPolicy function additionally stores an arbitrary policy ID without checking
that it exists, uses BLACKLIST semantics, or is administered by the proxy:
function initializeWithPolicy(address owner_, uint64 policyId_)
external initializer {
_transferOwnership(owner_);
_getPolicyAdminStorage().policyId = policyId_;
}
The policyExists modifier rejects only ID zero, while isFrozen assumes blacklist semantics. A
nonexistent, non-BLACKLIST, or incorrect-admin policy can make freeze/thaw revert or invert
isFrozen.
Impact
An authorized deployer can initialize either one-shot path with no local owner. The alternate path
can also bind an unusable policy, requiring a proxy upgrade or action by the actual policy
administrator to recover.
Reviewed production scripts use the normal initializer with a multi-signature owner. The issue
therefore requires a privileged deployment mistake, not an unprivileged call against an initialized
proxy.
Recommendations
Reject a zero owner in both initializers. For initializeWithPolicy, also reject policy ID zero and
require an existing BLACKLIST policy whose administrator is address(this).
