3.11.
Custom EIP-712 initializers omit the onlyInitializing guard
Target
EIP712Upgradeable
ID
ZELLIC-SA8P5Q
Category
Code Maturity
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
The custom upgradable EIP-712 module defines both initialization helpers without OpenZeppelin's
onlyInitializing modifier:
function __EIP712_init(string memory name, string memory version) internal {
__EIP712_init_unchained(name, version);
}
function __EIP712_init_unchained(string memory name, string memory version)
internal {
EIP712Storage storage $ = _getEIP712Storage();
$._name = name;
$._version = version;
$._hashedName = 0;
$._hashedVersion = 0;
}
These helpers rewrite the EIP-712 domain and reset its cached hashes. Standard upgradable
modules restrict equivalent writes to an active initializer or reinitializer.
Every reviewed call site, at the time of writing, is inside reinitializer(3) or reinitializer(4),
and neither helper is ABI-exposed.
Impact
No unprivileged path invokes these helpers outside initialization. The omission instead weakens
the inheritance contract: future derived code could expose a call that changes the signature
domain and invalidates or changes verification of outstanding permit and EIP-3009 authorizations.
This is upgrade hardening, not a vulnerability in the reviewed call surface.
Zellic © 2026
←Back to Contents
Page 37 of 505

frxUSD Ecosystem Smart Contract Security Assessment
October 19, 2026
Recommendations
Add onlyInitializing to both helpers:
function __EIP712_init(string memory name, string memory version)
internal
onlyInitializing
{
__EIP712_init_unchained(name, version);
}
function __EIP712_init_unchained(string memory name, string memory version)
internal
onlyInitializing
{
// Existing storage writes.
}
Retain the guarded external reinitializer functions. Test that initialization succeeds inside them and
that a derived external call outside an initialization context reverts.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Frax, and a fix was implemented in commit 22f00aac ↗.
