3.14.
Administrator transitions can strand principal awaiting compose settlement
Target
RemoteHopV201Tempo and HopV201Tempo
ID
ZELLIC-CWSWST
Category
Protocol Risks
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
The destination OFT credits a compose recipient before queueing lzCompose for a separate
transaction. For composed hop transfers, RemoteHopV201Tempo therefore holds principal
between destination credit and compose execution:
uint256 amountReceivedLD = _credit(toAddress, _toLD(message.amountSD()),
origin.srcEid);
endpoint.sendCompose(toAddress, guid, 0, composeMsg);
Several privileged operations cross this interval:
• The recoverERC20 function can transfer underlying tokens without reserving balances
for queued compose messages.
• The setMessageProcessed function can pre-mark the pending tuple; compose then
returns as a duplicate and finalizes without recipient payment.
• OFT deapproval or pause makes compose revert until restored.
• Replacing remoteHop(srcEid) changes sender interpretation for an already credited
message and can make strict recipient authentication revert.
The hop has no pending-GUID reservation or claim ledger tying pooled balances to queued
messages.
Impact
Recovery can underfund a pending transfer; replay pre-marking is terminal for automatic retry
because compose returns success; and configuration changes can delay settlement until
governance restores prior state.
All triggers are privileged. Governance can replenish, restore, or compensate manually, so this is a
custody and operational-settlement boundary rather than a permissionless drain.
Zellic © 2026
←Back to Contents
Page 43 of 505

frxUSD Ecosystem Smart Contract Security Assessment
October 19, 2026
Recommendations
Track pending claims and reconcile them before recovery, replay pre-marking, OFT deapproval, or
remote-hop replacement. Preserve immediate emergency pause and revocation, but define an
explicit retry, cancellation, or compensation process.
For on-chain enforcement, reserve amounts by authenticated pending GUID and version
trusted-hop configuration for queued messages. Keep a claim-aware emergency recovery path; a
blanket token-recovery ban would also block refunds for genuinely failed compose messages.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Frax, and a fix was implemented in commit 79ecfc5a ↗.
