3.16.
Executable OFT sends do not enforce the shared-decimal ceiling
Target
Frax OFT implementations and adapters
ID
ZELLIC-BFHKMW
Category
Integration Risks
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
OFT messages encode transfer amounts in a uint64 shared-decimal field. The inherited
conversion narrows the value without checking representability:
function _toSD(uint256 amountLD) internal view returns (uint64 amountSD) {
return uint64(amountLD / decimalConversionRate);
}
The reviewed OFTs and adapters advertise _toLD(type(uint64).max) as
quoteOFT().oftLimit.maxAmountLD, but _debitView does not enforce it. A send can burn, lock,
or ledger-account the full local-decimal amount before message encoding retains only the low 64
shared-decimal bits. At exactly 2**64 shared units, the payload amount wraps to zero while the
source receipt reports the full amount.
Slippage does not close the gap: _debitView checks _minAmountLD against the full dust-trimmed
amount before narrowing. The quoteSend function prices the truncated packet, while
mintable-adapter accounting records the full source amount.
Impact
An oversized sender can lose its full source amount while the destination receives only the
truncated value. The source receipt and transfer ledger retain the full amount, while the fee quote
corresponds to the truncated packet.
Reachability is remote. At six shared decimals, the first unrepresentable amount is
18,446,744,073,709.551616 whole tokens. The proof of concept required a public-mint mock, while
sampled frxUSD supply was about 89.8 million. Only the initiating sender's balance is debited.
Zellic © 2026
←Back to Contents
Page 47 of 505

frxUSD Ecosystem Smart Contract Security Assessment
October 19, 2026
Recommendations
Before narrowing, reject any amount for which amountReceivedLD / decimalConversionRate >
type(uint64).max. Make quoteOFT, quoteSend, and send agree at the exact boundary.
A checked common _toSD path is sufficient for safety because a revert rolls back the earlier debit;
an earlier _debitView check also avoids wasted gas. Keep the change compact, and verify linked
