3.17.
Rebinding try-catch catches every revert from quoteSend()
Target
RemoteMintRedeemHopTempo
ID
ZELLIC-2AJ02J
Category
Code Maturity
Severity
Informational
Likelihood
N/A
Impact
Informational
Description
The _quoteSendRebindingOnFailure() function quotes the OFT through a try-catch. It is meant
to recover when LayerZero has delisted the hop contract's own FeeManager fee token (whichever
token the previous call paid with), which makes the OFT's quote validation revert.
try IOFT(_oft).quoteSend(_sendParam, false) returns (MessagingFee memory _fee)
{
return _fee;
} catch {
_bindFeeToken(_feeToken);
return IOFT(_oft).quoteSend(_sendParam, false);
}
The catch block has no condition, so it runs for any revert from quoteSend(). That includes
failures unrelated to the fee-token binding, such as a missing peer, an unset enforced option, or a
misconfigured OFT. For these failures, the function still calls _bindFeeToken(_feeToken). The
_bindFeeToken() function makes a userTokens read and, if the token differs, a setUserToken
write to the FeeManager precompile.
In the four-argument mintRedeem(), _feeToken is supplied by the caller. The contract's persistent
fee token is therefore temporarily set to a token the caller chose, before it is known whether the
binding was the cause. The second quoteSend() then fails again for the same unrelated reason,
and the whole transaction reverts, which undoes the binding.
Impact
No state change persists and no funds are at risk because a failing call reverts as a whole. These
are the costs:
• Every call that fails for an unrelated reason wastes gas on the precompile calls and a
second quoteSend().
• The caller sees the error from the second quote, not the first.
