Description
The targeted contracts override the preview* functions to skip fees when _isFeeExempt()
returns true. That helper keys on the caller, not on any account passed as an argument:
function _isFeeExempt() internal view returns (bool _isExempt) {
_isExempt = feeExempt[msg.sender] || feeExempt[tx.origin];
}
The FrxUSDCustodianBase and FrxUSDCustodian contracts build their limit functions on these
previews:
function maxWithdraw(address _owner)
public view returns (uint256 _maxAssetsOut) {
uint256 _maxAssetsUser = previewRedeem(frxUSD.balanceOf(address(_owner)));
...
}
The maxRedeem function uses previewWithdraw, and maxDeposit uses previewMint. As a result,
these limits use the exemption status of the caller, not of _owner. A fee-exempt caller sees the full
pre-fee value from maxWithdraw(_owner). A non-exempt caller querying the same _owner sees a
value reduced by redeemFee. The NatSpec on these functions says only ""Includes fee"" and does
not mention that the result depends on the caller.
The on-chain flow stays consistent. The withdraw and redeem functions require _owner ==
msg.sender, so the limit they check matches the caller's actual fee treatment. The mismatch
appears only when a third party reads the value, for example an integrator contract, a router, or an
off-chain eth_call made from a different from address.
