frxUSD Ecosystem Smart Contract Security Assessment
October 19, 2026
Impact
No funds are at risk, and there is no incorrect state transition. Integrators and front ends that call
maxWithdraw, maxRedeem, maxDeposit, or maxMint on behalf of a user may get a value that differs
from what the user would see when calling directly. For example, a nonexempt integrator contract
will see a fee-adjusted maxWithdraw for an exempt user's balance.
Recommendations
Document in the NatSpec of maxWithdraw, maxRedeem, maxDeposit, and maxMint that the returned
values depend on the fee-exemption status of the caller (msg.sender or tx.origin). Optionally,
evaluate the exemption against _owner inside the max* functions so that their results depend only
on the queried account.
Remediation
This issue has been acknowledged by Frax.
